WEBVTT


00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:34.397
English sub by inSanos


00:00:34.398 --> 00:00:36.867
Transcribed from audio by: anreith


00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.337
Timing by: coas and Resynk by: Engeln29


00:01:29.842 --> 00:01:31.843
MEGA DENG COOPER MINE, INDIA


00:01:37.405 --> 00:01:39.480
Watch out, watch out!


00:01:42.932 --> 00:01:45.021
Welcome my friend!


00:01:45.242 --> 00:01:47.444
- Great to see you!
- Glad you made it


00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:49.927
This can't be Ajit.


00:01:49.928 --> 00:01:52.490
He's a little man
already. Unbelievable.


00:01:52.491 --> 00:01:53.935
I hope you're
hungry, Adrian.


00:01:54.032 --> 00:01:56.112
I'm famished. How
are you, Aparna?


00:01:56.113 --> 00:01:57.752
I made that fish
curry you love.


00:01:58.075 --> 00:01:59.352
I can't wait.


00:01:59.736 --> 00:02:01.528
She gets more beautiful
every time I see her,


00:02:01.529 --> 00:02:02.324
Why is that?


00:02:02.325 --> 00:02:03.453
Strange, isn't it?


00:02:03.454 --> 00:02:06.053
But her fish curry
is still awful.


00:02:07.118 --> 00:02:08.949
You were mysterious
on the phone.


00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.393
Why didn't you attend
the conference?


00:02:10.573 --> 00:02:12.031
I will show you, Adrian, sir.


00:02:12.032 --> 00:02:14.161
Satnam. Stop sir-ing me.


00:02:20.816 --> 00:02:22.371
How deep do we need to go?


00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.148
11.000 feet.


00:02:24.904 --> 00:02:26.791
Searched all over India
for this dig.


00:02:27.949 --> 00:02:29.996
Used to be the deepest
copper mine in the world.


00:02:34.798 --> 00:02:37.053
Remember my brother Gurdeep?
He's a student now.


00:02:37.311 --> 00:02:38.826
Namaste, Dr Helmsley, sir.


00:02:39.229 --> 00:02:40.881
Adrian. It's just Adrian.


00:02:43.756 --> 00:02:45.422
Just don't pour too much, okay?


00:02:47.952 --> 00:02:49.488
How do you work
in this heat?


00:02:50.502 --> 00:02:51.933
You've come on a good
day, my friend.


00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.144
Sometimes it can
be 120° F.


00:02:55.648 --> 00:02:57.141
I want you to meet
Dr Lokesh?


00:02:57.373 --> 00:02:59.647
Fellow of Quantum Physics
at the University in Chennai


00:02:59.648 --> 00:03:01.283
- Namaste
- Dr Helmsley


00:03:04.261 --> 00:03:06.487
So, what are we
looking at?


00:03:06.488 --> 00:03:09.671
These neutrinos are
acting normally. No mass,


00:03:09.672 --> 00:03:11.787
no electrical charge.
They pass through


00:03:11.788 --> 00:03:13.481
ordinary matter
almost undisturbed.


00:03:13.482 --> 00:03:14.727
Your message said
the count doubled


00:03:14.728 --> 00:03:16.772
after the last
solar eruptions.


00:03:17.027 --> 00:03:18.406
That was last week.


00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.665
But this happened
two days ago.


00:03:26.598 --> 00:03:29.625
The biggest solar eruptions
in human history.


00:03:29.904 --> 00:03:31.683
Causing the highest
neutrino count


00:03:31.684 --> 00:03:32.836
we've ever recorded.


00:03:33.611 --> 00:03:35.359
My God.


00:03:38.432 --> 00:03:40.429
That's not what
worries me, Adrian.


00:03:41.034 --> 00:03:42.726
For the first time ever


00:03:44.242 --> 00:03:46.742
the neutrinos are causing
a physical reaction


00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.578
That's impossible.


00:03:54.039 --> 00:03:55.119
Ah!


00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.289
That feels very good!


00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.551
Please, follow me.


00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:05.947
You wont believe this.


00:04:08.251 --> 00:04:11.081
This water tank goes
down another 6000 feet.


00:04:12.575 --> 00:04:14.911
It looks like the neutrinos
coming from the sun


00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.831
have mutated into a new
kind of nuclear particle.


00:04:25.281 --> 00:04:27.262
They're heating up
the Earth's core.


00:04:28.199 --> 00:04:30.268
And suddenly act
like microwaves.


00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.492
Ladies and gentlemen.
As promised:


00:04:44.165 --> 00:04:46.434
No speech!


00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:48.747
Just a "thank you".


00:04:48.748 --> 00:04:51.493
Because tonight, with your
extraordinary generosity,


00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:55.802
we have raised
1.7 million dollars.


00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.718
It's okay.


00:05:01.719 --> 00:05:03.999
- I work for the White House.
- I don't care who you are, sir


00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.677
This is a black tie event.


00:05:05.879 --> 00:05:07.189
Scotty!


00:05:08.031 --> 00:05:10.551
Hey, Adrian, I thought
you were in India


00:05:10.552 --> 00:05:11.452
What's going on?


00:05:11.453 --> 00:05:13.103
- I need your jacket
- What?


00:05:13.199 --> 00:05:14.076
I gotta speak
to Anheuser


00:05:14.077 --> 00:05:15.476
- I don't wanna give...
- Give me your damn jacket!


00:05:15.477 --> 00:05:17.003
Take it, please.


00:05:23.048 --> 00:05:25.709
Easy! That's a
600 dollar jacket.


00:05:26.654 --> 00:05:27.979
Mr Anheuser?


00:05:28.552 --> 00:05:29.940
Mr Anheuser?


00:05:30.957 --> 00:05:32.435
I need to talk to you.


00:05:35.679 --> 00:05:36.618
Do I know you?


00:05:36.619 --> 00:05:38.430
Sorry sir, my name is
Dr Adrian Helmsley


00:05:38.431 --> 00:05:39.839
I'm a deputy geologist
at the Office of


00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.943
Science and Technology Policy


00:05:42.965 --> 00:05:44.538
Excuse me, fellows.


00:05:45.266 --> 00:05:47.370
You know that this
is a fund-raiser,


00:05:47.371 --> 00:05:48.648
not a frat party, right?


00:05:48.649 --> 00:05:50.217
It's extremely
important, sir.


00:05:50.218 --> 00:05:51.956
It always is. Here is
what I want you to do:


00:05:51.957 --> 00:05:53.790
Make an appointment
or even better,


00:05:53.791 --> 00:05:56.400
Have your boss bring it up at
the quarterly science briefing


00:05:56.433 --> 00:05:57.710
There's a good plan.


00:05:58.638 --> 00:06:01.008
I just traveled 20 straight
hours to get here, sir.


00:06:01.009 --> 00:06:04.075
I haven't slept in two days.
You need to read this, sir.


00:06:04.076 --> 00:06:05.765
You need to read it now!


00:06:11.108 --> 00:06:14.173
Let me guess.
National geology crisis?


00:06:15.464 --> 00:06:16.637
Excuse me.


00:06:33.927 --> 00:06:35.079
Who do you
report to?


00:06:35.312 --> 00:06:36.568
Lico Vasos


00:06:36.569 --> 00:06:38.098
Not anymore.


00:06:40.844 --> 00:06:42.578
Al, bring the car around.


00:06:43.728 --> 00:06:45.494
You may wish you
took a shower.


00:06:45.495 --> 00:06:47.118
You're about to meet
the president.


00:06:47.445 --> 00:06:48.554
What's going on?


00:06:48.893 --> 00:06:50.675
Get that to the office.


00:07:07.472 --> 00:07:09.322
G8 SUMMIT, BRITISH COLUMBIA


00:07:19.363 --> 00:07:20.639
Good morning.


00:07:20.736 --> 00:07:22.320
I would like to
meet privately


00:07:22.321 --> 00:07:24.119
with my fellow
heads of state.


00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.333
Mr <name> wishes to have
his interpreters present.


00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:32.487
Mr President,
I can assure you


00:07:32.488 --> 00:07:34.881
Your English is more
than sufficient


00:07:34.882 --> 00:07:37.060
for what I have to say.


00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:57.709
Mr President.


00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:04.555
Six months ago, I was
made aware of a


00:08:04.556 --> 00:08:08.799
situation so devastating
that at first


00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.869
I refused to believe it.


00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.969
However,


00:08:13.194 --> 00:08:15.518
through the concerted efforts


00:08:15.519 --> 00:08:18.120
of our brightest scientists,


00:08:18.402 --> 00:08:21.797
we have confirmed its validity.


00:08:24.032 --> 00:08:29.213
The world
as we know it


00:08:29.214 --> 00:08:31.480
will soon come
to an end.


00:08:33.664 --> 00:08:35.851
CHO MING VALLEY, TIBET


00:08:39.909 --> 00:08:43.229
This dam project will create
many new jobs.


00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:48.411
The Party and Country will
assist in your re-location.


00:08:50.694 --> 00:08:52.221
Grandma, give me
your hand.


00:08:52.222 --> 00:08:53.592
But where are
they taking us?


00:08:53.593 --> 00:08:55.062
It'll be alright.


00:08:59.661 --> 00:09:00.903
Brother!


00:09:01.354 --> 00:09:03.796
Grandma, I will send you money.


00:09:09.409 --> 00:09:11.039
Who can write?


00:09:11.136 --> 00:09:12.667
Who can read?


00:09:14.132 --> 00:09:15.783
Who can weld?


00:09:28.088 --> 00:09:30.018
EMPIRE GRAND HOTEL, LONDON


00:09:46.515 --> 00:09:47.981
Has His Highness
had an opportunity


00:09:47.982 --> 00:09:50.071
to study the dossier?


00:09:54.297 --> 00:09:58.549
You must understand
I have a big family, Mr...


00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.093
Isaacs.


00:10:00.456 --> 00:10:03.441
One billion dollars is
a lot of money.


00:10:03.735 --> 00:10:06.563
I'm afraid the amount
is in Euros,


00:10:06.564 --> 00:10:08.219
Your Highness.


00:10:11.331 --> 00:10:13.642
MUSÉE DU LOUVRE, PARIS


00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:27.278
I put a lot of faith into
your organization.


00:10:28.501 --> 00:10:31.098
It's a perfect
replica, Roland.


00:10:31.099 --> 00:10:33.604
There are too many
fanatics out there


00:10:33.605 --> 00:10:35.003
that could damage her.


00:10:35.004 --> 00:10:36.788
Just think about
the beautiful


00:10:36.789 --> 00:10:39.649
Buddha statues they
blew up in Afghanistan.


00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:42.870
Our Heritage Organization
has already made selections


00:10:42.871 --> 00:10:46.983
from the British Museum
and Hermitage.


00:10:53.481 --> 00:10:56.431
I guess she'll be safe now,
tucked away.


00:10:56.528 --> 00:11:01.812
Hidden, in some bunker
in Switzerland.


00:11:02.546 --> 00:11:05.088
Perfectly safe, Roland.


00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:09.580
Only infrared analysis can
reveal the difference.


00:11:10.413 --> 00:11:12.490
But it's still a fake.


00:11:25.614 --> 00:11:29.051
<i>This mass suicide was actually
discovered by a documentary crew</i>


00:11:29.052 --> 00:11:31.425
<i>here in the ancient
Mayan city of Takal</i>


00:11:31.426 --> 00:11:33.449
<i>Now the victims,
and we've seen many,</i>


00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.752
<i>are said to have adhered
to the Mayan-Quiche calender,</i>


00:11:35.785 --> 00:11:37.934
<i>which predicts the
end of time to occur</i>


00:11:37.935 --> 00:11:40.448
<i>on the 21st December
of this year,</i>


00:11:40.449 --> 00:11:42.805
<i>due to the suns
destructive forces.</i>


00:11:42.806 --> 00:11:43.643
<i>Thank you, Mark.</i>


00:11:43.766 --> 00:11:46.683
<i>Strangely enough, scientific
records do support the fact</i>


00:11:46.684 --> 00:11:49.182
<i>that we are heading for
the biggest solar climax</i>


00:11:49.183 --> 00:11:51.179
<i>in recorded history.</i>


00:11:52.524 --> 00:11:55.099
MANHATTAN BEACH, CALIFORNIA


00:11:57.241 --> 00:11:59.948
<i>Many people believe
that the Mayan Calender</i>


00:11:59.949 --> 00:12:03.001
<i>predicts that there's supposed
to be a galactic alignment...</i>


00:12:03.193 --> 00:12:04.542
I'm a dead man.


00:12:16.471 --> 00:12:20.083
Hey, Kate, I'm practically
on the freeway right now.


00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:23.572
Yes, I'm rolling towards
you as we speak.


00:12:24.098 --> 00:12:27.074
Would you relax?
I'll be there any second.


00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:30.969
You know it's a vacation and not
a doctors appointment, right?


00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.585
It's supposed to be fun.


00:12:32.586 --> 00:12:34.647
You remember fun,
don't you Kate?


00:12:34.648 --> 00:12:35.569
Do you remember
where you were


00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.887
when it stopped
being fun for you?


00:12:39.873 --> 00:12:41.035
Got it.


00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:46.754
Bug spray?


00:12:47.019 --> 00:12:49.782
Oh yeah, cause it's mosquito
season in Yellowstone.


00:12:49.817 --> 00:12:53.674
I got a whole bunch. I gotta go,
I'm in a bad reception area.


00:13:00.621 --> 00:13:03.546
Woah, man. Would you
look at that?


00:13:03.738 --> 00:13:05.280
Sick


00:13:10.634 --> 00:13:12.348
Merrill, I told you.


00:13:12.349 --> 00:13:15.285
We have to move back
to Wisconsin.


00:13:15.382 --> 00:13:18.921
<i>These little mini-quakes are
really getting on my nerves, Randy.</i>


00:13:18.922 --> 00:13:21.449
<i>Come on, a little surface crack, you're
not gonna be inconvenienced by that</i>


00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.808
<i>Surface cracks, I've got a
plastic surgeon for that</i>


00:13:23.809 --> 00:13:27.145
<i>No kidding. Thank God for
those shake-proof coffee mugs.</i>


00:13:27.146 --> 00:13:29.060
<i>They show the true nature
of us Californians.</i>


00:13:29.061 --> 00:13:32.874
<i>We'll not bow to these little
inconvenient things like surface quakes.</i>


00:13:32.875 --> 00:13:34.738
<i>Do you have a funny mini-quake
story and want to share it?</i>


00:13:34.739 --> 00:13:35.699
<i>Call Lisa & Randy at 555...</i>


00:13:45.202 --> 00:13:46.792
- Hi daddy!
- Hi baby


00:13:46.793 --> 00:13:49.077
- How are you sweety?
- Good


00:13:49.078 --> 00:13:52.067
Jackson, what is this?
- Please don't call me that.


00:13:52.068 --> 00:13:53.663
I'm your dad.


00:13:55.204 --> 00:13:57.314
Taking them camping
in a limo?


00:13:57.819 --> 00:14:01.065
Okay, great. What happened
to your temp job?


00:14:01.748 --> 00:14:03.720
Better hours, more
time to write.


00:14:04.171 --> 00:14:06.317
What about sleeping, have you
been doing that lately?


00:14:06.318 --> 00:14:08.305
I've said it a
thousand times.


00:14:08.306 --> 00:14:10.969
No lipo on Fridays.
It's too messy.


00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:12.134
Hold on.


00:14:12.135 --> 00:14:13.388
- Morning Jackson.
- Hi


00:14:13.389 --> 00:14:15.240
- Nice ride.
- Thanks.


00:14:15.241 --> 00:14:18.642
Have a nice trip. Remember,
watch out for the bears.


00:14:18.735 --> 00:14:20.740
- Bye, Gordon
- Love you, Honey.


00:14:20.741 --> 00:14:21.595
Bye


00:14:21.596 --> 00:14:24.586
Okay, so...
- You tell him.


00:14:24.995 --> 00:14:25.959
Tell me what?


00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.722
She needs to put these on every
night before she goes to sleep.


00:14:28.723 --> 00:14:29.925
Still?


00:14:29.926 --> 00:14:32.041
Yes. Your 7 year old daughter
still wets her bed.


00:14:32.042 --> 00:14:33.918
Maybe that's something
you should know.


00:14:33.919 --> 00:14:35.890
- Love you
- Love you, Mom.


00:14:36.567 --> 00:14:38.246
- Hey
- You okay?


00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.161
They really were looking forward
to spending some time with you


00:14:43.196 --> 00:14:43.793
I know.


00:14:43.794 --> 00:14:45.753
So don't be on your
computer all the time.


00:14:45.788 --> 00:14:46.869
Got it.


00:14:50.817 --> 00:14:52.399
Love you!


00:14:56.303 --> 00:14:59.146
- So this time we'll hit Japan.
- So?


00:14:59.147 --> 00:15:01.243
Now you can visit
your boy, Will.


00:15:01.244 --> 00:15:02.588
Afternoon, ladies!


00:15:04.253 --> 00:15:05.600
Are you even
listening to me?


00:15:05.601 --> 00:15:07.697
Unfortunately I am, Harry.


00:15:07.732 --> 00:15:09.699
I heard from Audrey you're
a grandpa now.


00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.903
Would you mind keeping your
nose out of my family?


00:15:11.904 --> 00:15:15.105
You're cramping my style, baby.
There we are.


00:15:15.106 --> 00:15:18.318
So he married a Japanese girl,
how's that the end of the world?


00:15:18.319 --> 00:15:20.464
Come on Tony, you should
at least go see him.


00:15:20.465 --> 00:15:23.511
- You see your boy?
- Not as much as I'd like


00:15:23.512 --> 00:15:25.882
DC is a long way, but
at least we talk


00:15:25.883 --> 00:15:27.551
About what?


00:15:27.552 --> 00:15:30.751
Life.
And how short it is.


00:15:52.598 --> 00:15:55.531
What the hell was that?


00:16:01.188 --> 00:16:04.091
- Hello?
- Laura?


00:16:04.092 --> 00:16:05.739
<i>Laura, can you hear me?</i>


00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:07.273
Roland, is that you?


00:16:07.274 --> 00:16:09.807
<i>Laura, they lied to us.</i>


00:16:09.808 --> 00:16:11.948
I've arranged a press
conference for tomorrow.


00:16:11.949 --> 00:16:14.288
I will tell everyone the truth
about what is going on.


00:16:14.289 --> 00:16:15.933
<i>What are you talking about?</i>


00:16:15.934 --> 00:16:18.026
The art you collected


00:16:18.027 --> 00:16:20.007
is not in the Alps.


00:16:20.008 --> 00:16:21.462
<i>Those tunnels are empty.</i>


00:16:21.463 --> 00:16:22.809
<i>I have proof!</i>


00:16:25.184 --> 00:16:27.163
Laura, can you hear me?


00:16:27.164 --> 00:16:29.257
I'm losing you, Roland.


00:16:29.258 --> 00:16:30.881
Laura, can you hear me?


00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.334
YELLOWSTONE
NATIONAL PARK


00:17:00.104 --> 00:17:02.093
- I liked that song.
- We lost it.


00:17:02.094 --> 00:17:05.336
<i>...the west coast with
all those surface cracks,</i>


00:17:05.337 --> 00:17:08.888
<i>I told myself: Charlie,
get your stupid ass</i>


00:17:08.923 --> 00:17:10.081
<i>to Yellowstone.</i>


00:17:10.082 --> 00:17:13.692
<i>I don't want to miss all the
fun when it finally goes.</i>


00:17:13.693 --> 00:17:16.119
<i>Let me tell you, there's been
government people flying</i>


00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:21.325
<i>in and out all morning and
trust me, they do not look happy.</i>


00:17:21.326 --> 00:17:23.830
Always remember, folks...
- It's weird.


00:17:23.831 --> 00:17:26.996
Can you believe
he said that?


00:17:26.997 --> 00:17:29.087
What are the odds?


00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:31.504
We're not seeing the soil
liquefaction we'd expect


00:17:31.505 --> 00:17:33.306
or any evidence of
fracture propagation


00:17:33.307 --> 00:17:34.476
within the tectonic plates.


00:17:34.477 --> 00:17:36.413
- English, doctor.
- The seismic activity


00:17:36.414 --> 00:17:38.453
on the west coast is
not caused by tect...


00:17:38.454 --> 00:17:40.957
regular earth quakes.
And these surface cracks


00:17:40.958 --> 00:17:43.017
have nothing to do
with shifting fault lines.


00:17:43.018 --> 00:17:45.118
Are you suggesting this
could be the beginning


00:17:45.119 --> 00:17:47.529
of the Joline operation?
- Dr Helmsley is flying to


00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:49.508
Yellowstone to collect
more data, sir.


00:17:49.509 --> 00:17:53.720
We've been following the schedule
you established, Mr Helmsley.


00:17:53.721 --> 00:17:55.922
The most important schedule
in the history of mankind.


00:17:55.923 --> 00:17:58.941
Now you're telling me we
have to throw it out?


00:17:58.942 --> 00:17:59.902
Yes, sir.


00:18:01.767 --> 00:18:03.710
I was wrong.


00:18:06.846 --> 00:18:08.024
Do you know how
many times I've heard


00:18:08.025 --> 00:18:10.024
those words
in this office?


00:18:10.664 --> 00:18:12.630
Zero.


00:18:14.309 --> 00:18:15.289
Did you see this?


00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.558
I'm sorry Mr President.
She insisted.


00:18:17.559 --> 00:18:19.306
It's all over the news.


00:18:22.329 --> 00:18:25.332
<i>We are learning more about
this deadly car explosion,</i>


00:18:25.333 --> 00:18:27.554
<i>The director of the French
National Museum</i>


00:18:27.555 --> 00:18:29.640
<i>was scheduled to hold
a press conference at</i>


00:18:29.641 --> 00:18:30.792
<i>the Louvre this morning.</i>


00:18:30.793 --> 00:18:34.752
<i>Coincidentally, his death took
place in the same Paris tunnel</i>


00:18:34.753 --> 00:18:37.910
<i>where Princess Diana
died in 1997.</i>


00:18:37.911 --> 00:18:41.081
<i>We are continuing to
follow this story...</i>


00:18:41.116 --> 00:18:45.908
Laura, I don't believe
you've met Dr Helmsley.


00:18:45.909 --> 00:18:48.100
I just talked to him Dad,
and he told me...


00:18:48.101 --> 00:18:49.937
the organization I
work for is a sham.


00:18:49.938 --> 00:18:51.663
Why would he say that?


00:18:55.979 --> 00:18:58.351
You look just like your mother
when you get upset.


00:18:58.352 --> 00:19:02.059
- Did I ever tell you that?
- Every time I get upset.


00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:05.434
Daddy, a man was killed.


00:19:06.183 --> 00:19:09.682
Honey. Please sit down.


00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:21.150
Only a dozen people
in this administration


00:19:21.151 --> 00:19:22.974
know what I'm
about to tell you.


00:19:23.208 --> 00:19:25.421
Dad, what's going on?


00:19:28.961 --> 00:19:31.974
An unprecedented
international endeavor


00:19:31.975 --> 00:19:32.935
is under way.


00:19:33.563 --> 00:19:38.312
At this point 46 nations
are invested in this thing.


00:19:38.313 --> 00:19:40.188
Laura's a smart girl.
She'll understand.


00:19:40.223 --> 00:19:42.021
That thing in Paris.


00:19:42.022 --> 00:19:43.966
We're not involved in
any of that, are we?


00:19:43.967 --> 00:19:45.824
"We"?
Who the hell is "we"?


00:19:45.825 --> 00:19:47.325
What are you
talking about?


00:19:47.442 --> 00:19:49.960
What we need to do is
focus on this time line.


00:19:49.961 --> 00:19:51.497
So when do we let
the country know?


00:19:51.498 --> 00:19:54.375
What do you mean?
- The people, sir.


00:19:54.376 --> 00:19:56.335
They need to know.


00:19:56.939 --> 00:19:59.732
Well of course
they do. Listen.


00:19:59.733 --> 00:20:03.128
Your job is to figure out when
this is all gonna fall apart.


00:20:03.163 --> 00:20:06.524
My job is to figure out how to
retain some type of government


00:20:06.525 --> 00:20:07.982
after it falls apart.


00:20:07.983 --> 00:20:09.853
Until then we don't have
time for anything


00:20:09.854 --> 00:20:11.897
except those jobs. Okay?


00:20:12.144 --> 00:20:15.553
Call me when you have
any news from Yellowstone.


00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:19.355
- Cute girl, huh?
- Sir?


00:20:19.356 --> 00:20:21.133
The First Daughter,
I saw you looking at her.


00:20:21.134 --> 00:20:24.298
- I wasn't looking at her
- Better move fast kid


00:20:24.299 --> 00:20:26.357
The end is near.


00:20:27.093 --> 00:20:28.599
Your chopper's ready.


00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:31.119
They're waiting
on the south lawn.


00:20:32.257 --> 00:20:37.526
- Daddy, where are we going?
- This special place I know


00:20:37.527 --> 00:20:39.186
Actually, it's a place
where your mom and I


00:20:39.187 --> 00:20:40.294
used to hang out a lot.


00:20:40.295 --> 00:20:42.629
I don't want to know
where you and mom had sex.


00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:43.914
I'm not ready
for that, Jackson.


00:20:43.915 --> 00:20:46.818
Stop calling me that,
it's creeping me out.


00:20:46.819 --> 00:20:48.388
What's wrong with "Dad"?


00:20:49.617 --> 00:20:51.494
Daddy, look at this.


00:20:51.805 --> 00:20:53.022
That wasn't here before.


00:20:54.223 --> 00:20:55.905
What did I do?


00:20:55.906 --> 00:20:57.988
Go get your hat.


00:21:02.229 --> 00:21:04.180
Can't you see the signs?


00:21:11.807 --> 00:21:13.708
There used to be
a lake here.


00:21:13.709 --> 00:21:15.964
Doesn't look much
of a lake to me.


00:21:15.965 --> 00:21:18.357
I know. The whole
damn thing's gone.


00:21:20.083 --> 00:21:21.291
Come on, let's
check it out.


00:21:21.292 --> 00:21:22.680
Great.


00:21:43.714 --> 00:21:46.748
Subjects have now
entered hot zone.


00:21:59.295 --> 00:22:00.694
What is that?


00:22:02.038 --> 00:22:03.992
It's the U.S. Army.


00:22:13.333 --> 00:22:14.981
All manner of
government vehicle


00:22:14.982 --> 00:22:17.005
are converging
on subjects.


00:22:17.198 --> 00:22:18.613
You're in a
restricted area, sir.


00:22:18.614 --> 00:22:20.220
We need you and your
family to come with us.


00:22:20.221 --> 00:22:23.727
Right. Okay, we're gonna
go with these guys.


00:22:23.728 --> 00:22:24.935
That'll be fun, huh?


00:22:28.133 --> 00:22:31.746
This is wild.
This is really wild.


00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:46.286
This is unbelievable.
2700° C at 40.000 feet?


00:22:46.287 --> 00:22:48.495
I know, it sounds
completely implausible.


00:22:48.496 --> 00:22:51.895
Nonetheless, we're noticing
an increase of almost 0.5%


00:22:51.896 --> 00:22:54.002
- Per day?
- No.


00:22:54.003 --> 00:22:54.817
Per hour.


00:22:54.818 --> 00:22:58.296
Dr Helmsley, we arrested
some tourists in the hot zone.


00:22:58.297 --> 00:22:59.319
I'll take care of it.


00:22:59.320 --> 00:23:02.686
Let's get Satnam on the
communications link.


00:23:02.687 --> 00:23:04.172
Cross reference the data.


00:23:04.173 --> 00:23:07.969
It's a national park, there's
not supposed to be fences.


00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:09.198
What's going on here?


00:23:09.199 --> 00:23:11.221
We're geologists.


00:23:11.646 --> 00:23:14.120
You usually go digging
with machine guns?


00:23:15.419 --> 00:23:17.366
Major, I'll take care
of this, thank you.


00:23:17.367 --> 00:23:18.696
So what happened
to the lake?


00:23:18.697 --> 00:23:20.636
Well that's what we're
trying to find out.


00:23:20.637 --> 00:23:22.362
We think the entire area
has become unstable.


00:23:22.363 --> 00:23:24.848
I think you should take
your kids and leave, Mr...


00:23:24.849 --> 00:23:26.092
Curtis.


00:23:27.271 --> 00:23:29.062
You're not by any chance
the Jackson Curtis who


00:23:29.097 --> 00:23:31.962
wrote "Farewell Atlantis"?


00:23:34.142 --> 00:23:35.331
The very same.


00:23:36.521 --> 00:23:39.121
It's actually dedicated
to my mom.


00:23:41.101 --> 00:23:44.839
I read a couple of your
short stories in college.


00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:47.664
Your father is a
very talented man


00:23:47.665 --> 00:23:48.257
Listen up.


00:23:48.258 --> 00:23:49.890
It's amazing.
I'm reading your book.


00:23:49.891 --> 00:23:51.918
I'm around day 300,
the shuttle has just


00:23:51.919 --> 00:23:53.145
lost communication
with Earth.


00:23:53.146 --> 00:23:55.051
You're one of the lucky
few who bought it.


00:23:55.052 --> 00:23:57.390
- I didn't buy it.
- No?


00:23:57.391 --> 00:23:59.329
My dad gave
it to me.


00:24:00.444 --> 00:24:02.662
Let me ask
you something.


00:24:02.663 --> 00:24:04.798
Do you think those people
would behave so selflessly


00:24:04.799 --> 00:24:07.101
knowing that their own
lives were at stake?


00:24:07.102 --> 00:24:08.936
I hope so.


00:24:08.971 --> 00:24:12.144
The critics said I was naive,
an unabashed optimist,


00:24:12.145 --> 00:24:13.788
but what do
they know, right?


00:24:16.067 --> 00:24:18.169
It was a great pleasure
meeting you.


00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:19.880
Mayor, could you escort
these good people


00:24:19.881 --> 00:24:20.888
to the camp
grounds, please.


00:24:20.889 --> 00:24:21.848
This is yours.


00:24:22.312 --> 00:24:23.283
- Thank you
- Yes, sir.


00:24:23.284 --> 00:24:25.297
- Take care.
- Okay


00:24:25.298 --> 00:24:26.324
He was very nice.


00:24:26.325 --> 00:24:28.588
You're just saying that
cause you like my book.


00:24:33.784 --> 00:24:35.336
Looks like that boy
of yours is gonna be


00:24:35.337 --> 00:24:36.653
smarter than any of us.


00:24:41.489 --> 00:24:42.759
What's wrong?


00:24:42.760 --> 00:24:45.724
I sent Satnam the
temperature readings.


00:24:45.725 --> 00:24:47.945
My colleagues in Argentina
and Ontario have


00:24:47.946 --> 00:24:49.769
almost identical data.


00:24:49.770 --> 00:24:52.059
It's so hot here we've
had to seal off the mine.


00:24:52.060 --> 00:24:53.127
Did you double check
the numbers?


00:24:53.162 --> 00:24:54.749
I triple checked,
my friend.


00:24:54.750 --> 00:24:57.164
I wish we were
wrong, but


00:24:57.165 --> 00:24:58.124
we're not.


00:24:59.344 --> 00:25:02.413
The Earth's crust is
destabilizing.


00:25:06.570 --> 00:25:07.724
It's too early.


00:25:07.759 --> 00:25:11.388
Adrian. You have to
begin the evacuation.


00:25:13.189 --> 00:25:14.817
My God.


00:25:14.818 --> 00:25:18.311
All our scientific advances,
our fancy machines,


00:25:18.312 --> 00:25:21.275
the Mayans saw this coming
thousands of years ago.


00:25:29.959 --> 00:25:32.358
I thought we'd
have more time.


00:25:39.880 --> 00:25:41.123
Okay.


00:25:41.592 --> 00:25:43.488
Okay, I want you to
pack up your family.


00:25:43.489 --> 00:25:46.083
I'm gonna arrange
an airlift from Delhi.


00:25:46.084 --> 00:25:48.028
Thank you my friend.


00:25:48.029 --> 00:25:49.919
And good luck.


00:25:58.137 --> 00:25:59.803
Ajit.


00:26:00.728 --> 00:26:02.779
We are going
on a big ship.


00:26:12.020 --> 00:26:14.502
Wait. Wait, wait.


00:26:14.537 --> 00:26:16.985
Sorry. One question.


00:26:16.986 --> 00:26:22.550
What did the government
guys say to you?


00:26:24.955 --> 00:26:27.626
They don't like us going
over their fences and


00:26:27.627 --> 00:26:31.008
that the whole area
back there is unstable.


00:26:31.009 --> 00:26:31.929
"Unstable"?


00:26:31.930 --> 00:26:34.234
They said "unstable"?


00:26:37.068 --> 00:26:38.683
That's funny.


00:26:38.684 --> 00:26:39.644
Let's go.


00:26:43.232 --> 00:26:45.548
"Unstable".


00:26:50.053 --> 00:26:51.964
It's not just
Yellowstone, sir.


00:26:51.965 --> 00:26:54.625
Temperatures are rising
with incredible velocity


00:26:54.626 --> 00:26:56.465
in hot zones across
the globe.


00:26:56.466 --> 00:26:58.979
Are you absolutely sure
about this, Adrian?


00:26:58.980 --> 00:27:02.845
Once we give these orders,
there's no going back.


00:27:02.846 --> 00:27:05.898
I'm afraid there's
no longer any doubt.


00:27:05.899 --> 00:27:07.711
We have to save
what we can.


00:27:07.712 --> 00:27:10.171
And we have
to move now!


00:27:38.594 --> 00:27:42.665
There's mosquitoes in here.
Did anybody spray the tent?


00:27:42.666 --> 00:27:44.736
I'm gonna get that
spray tomorrow.


00:27:44.737 --> 00:27:47.473
They just like you because
your blood's so sweet.


00:27:48.256 --> 00:27:50.936
Dad, you said you wouldn't
work on your book.


00:27:50.971 --> 00:27:51.825
What?


00:27:51.826 --> 00:27:54.875
I'm not, I'm doing
something else.


00:27:57.618 --> 00:27:59.096
Okay.


00:28:02.068 --> 00:28:03.830
Did you really need
all these hats?


00:28:03.831 --> 00:28:05.154
Where are
your pull-ups?


00:28:05.155 --> 00:28:06.682
I have them on.


00:28:13.948 --> 00:28:14.884
Who gave you this?
Mommy?


00:28:14.885 --> 00:28:17.705
No, Gordon gave it to me
for my birthday.


00:28:18.230 --> 00:28:20.344
A cell phone is something
we got to talk about


00:28:20.345 --> 00:28:21.305
As a family.


00:28:22.790 --> 00:28:24.722
What family?


00:28:27.976 --> 00:28:30.897
It hurts my feelings when
you say stuff like that.


00:28:33.027 --> 00:28:34.079
Go away.


00:28:39.079 --> 00:28:42.844
Adults get hurt feelings too.


00:28:59.486 --> 00:29:00.807
No way.


00:29:01.205 --> 00:29:02.004
<i>...tell the truth.</i>


00:29:02.005 --> 00:29:04.032
<i>Thank you, Bill.
What is your question?</i>


00:29:04.033 --> 00:29:06.735
<i>I wanted to know, where
is all this gonna start?</i>


00:29:06.736 --> 00:29:08.962
<i>Well, something like this could
only originate in Hollywood.</i>


00:29:08.963 --> 00:29:12.440
<i>They have the earth cracking
under their asses already.</i>


00:29:12.441 --> 00:29:15.138
<i>Our family believes in the
gospel of the lord Jesus.</i>


00:29:15.139 --> 00:29:16.454
<i>We have nothing
to fear, Charlie.</i>


00:29:16.455 --> 00:29:18.509
Good for you, Bill.
Thanks for calling.


00:29:18.736 --> 00:29:21.636
This is Charlie Frost
reporting live from


00:29:21.637 --> 00:29:25.071
Yellowstone National Park,
soon to become the worlds


00:29:25.072 --> 00:29:29.005
largest active volcano.


00:29:29.048 --> 00:29:31.094
I'll be right back, folks.


00:29:33.311 --> 00:29:35.357
Do you mind
if I join you?


00:29:35.358 --> 00:29:36.606
I wanted to ask
you something.


00:29:36.806 --> 00:29:40.389
I only got a minute.
Pickle?


00:29:41.595 --> 00:29:43.876
I was listening to the broadcast
and I was wondering


00:29:43.877 --> 00:29:47.425
what exactly is it that's
gonna start in Hollywood?


00:29:47.426 --> 00:29:51.352
It's the Apocalypse.
End of days.


00:29:51.406 --> 00:29:54.896
The Judgment Day. The end
of the world, my friend.


00:29:54.925 --> 00:29:57.654
Christians call it The Rapture,
but the Mayans


00:29:57.655 --> 00:29:59.597
knew about it, the Hopis,


00:29:59.598 --> 00:30:04.264
The I Ching, the Bible.


00:30:04.506 --> 00:30:07.040
- Beer?
- Yeah.


00:30:07.110 --> 00:30:08.773
So look, I gotta eat.


00:30:08.774 --> 00:30:11.453
Why don't you
download my blog?


00:30:11.454 --> 00:30:15.980
It's free. Of course, we do
appreciate donations.


00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:18.584
<i>In ancient times, the Mayan
people were the first</i>


00:30:18.585 --> 00:30:20.991
<i>civilization to discover
that this planet had</i>


00:30:20.992 --> 00:30:24.043
<i>an expiration date.
According to their calender,</i>


00:30:24.044 --> 00:30:27.671
<i>in the year 2012 a
cataclysmic event will unfold,</i>


00:30:27.672 --> 00:30:30.533
<i>caused by an alignment
of the planets in our solar system</i>


00:30:30.568 --> 00:30:34.701
<i>that only happens
every 640.000 years.</i>


00:30:34.702 --> 00:30:36.329
<i>Oh, not again.</i>


00:30:36.330 --> 00:30:40.483
Neat, huh? I did all
the animation myself.


00:30:40.520 --> 00:30:44.024
<i>Just imagine the earth
as an orange</i>


00:30:44.043 --> 00:30:47.159
You lure them in
with humor.


00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:48.499
Then you make
them think.


00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:51.803
<i>Our sun will begin to emit such
extreme amounts of radiation,</i>


00:30:51.827 --> 00:30:54.167
<i>Screw you bastards.</i>


00:30:54.168 --> 00:30:56.499
<i>That the core of the earth
will melt at the inside</i>


00:30:56.500 --> 00:30:57.460
<i>part of the orange.</i>


00:30:57.742 --> 00:31:00.625
<i>Leaving the crust of our
planet free to shift.</i>


00:31:00.653 --> 00:31:04.020
<i>In 1958 Professor Charles
Hapgood named it:</i>


00:31:04.055 --> 00:31:04.989
<i>"Earth Crust Displacement"</i>


00:31:05.024 --> 00:31:08.593
<i>Albert Einstein
did support it.</i>


00:31:08.619 --> 00:31:11.242
<i>People will get it all, the
forces of Mother Nature</i>


00:31:11.243 --> 00:31:14.094
<i>will be so devastating
It will bring an end to</i>


00:31:14.095 --> 00:31:18.651
<i>this world on winter
Solstice 12-21-12.</i>


00:31:18.679 --> 00:31:21.687
<i>Always remember, folks.
You heard it first from</i>


00:31:21.722 --> 00:31:22.838
<i>Charlie Frost.</i>


00:31:23.428 --> 00:31:26.486
You'd have to keep a thing
like this under wraps.


00:31:26.487 --> 00:31:27.996
Just think about it.


00:31:28.123 --> 00:31:30.884
First, the stock market would go.


00:31:30.885 --> 00:31:33.154
Then the economy: Boom!


00:31:33.155 --> 00:31:34.372
The dollar: Boom!


00:31:34.407 --> 00:31:36.558
And then pandemonium
in the street.


00:31:36.559 --> 00:31:40.342
War, genocide.
Boom Boom Boom!


00:31:40.343 --> 00:31:43.592
Bullshit. Nobody could keep
that big a secret, Charlie.


00:31:43.593 --> 00:31:44.485
Somebody would blow
the whistle


00:31:44.486 --> 00:31:48.331
An every once in a while,
some poor sucker tries.


00:31:48.332 --> 00:31:50.825
Like these guys.
Boom! Boom!


00:31:50.860 --> 00:31:54.660
Every one of these
guys: Dead! Dead! Dead!


00:31:56.204 --> 00:31:59.570
Woah, that's
Professor Meyers.


00:31:59.602 --> 00:32:01.710
He ran the Atlantis
Shuttle Program.


00:32:01.711 --> 00:32:02.607
Did you know him?


00:32:02.642 --> 00:32:04.639
- Yeah, he helped me out
with research on my book.


00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:07.668
Well, that must have been
before his accident.


00:32:07.692 --> 00:32:11.417
- Meyers is dead?
- Yeah, two months ago.


00:32:11.452 --> 00:32:14.787
He was one of my
most avid listeners.


00:32:14.819 --> 00:32:16.120
He had it all figured out.


00:32:16.121 --> 00:32:19.737
Everything the government
was doing, where, why.


00:32:19.738 --> 00:32:22.585
He even sent me a map.


00:32:22.623 --> 00:32:26.481
A map for what, Charlie?
What's the map for?


00:32:31.591 --> 00:32:36.624
They're building
space ships, man.


00:32:41.368 --> 00:32:47.104
Shit, man, I have to go.
I gotta get back to Earth.


00:32:47.128 --> 00:32:49.805
- Do you have a beer?
- This is my last.


00:32:49.806 --> 00:32:52.867
- Alright, I really enjoyed
most of this.


00:32:52.868 --> 00:32:55.696
Thank you so much.


00:32:55.697 --> 00:32:57.543
- Guess what, they're
selling seats!


00:32:57.544 --> 00:32:58.543
- Put me down for three.


00:32:58.544 --> 00:33:00.984
- No! Guys like you and me
don't have any chance.


00:33:00.985 --> 00:33:03.640
You'd have to be Bill Gates
or Rupert Murdoch


00:33:03.641 --> 00:33:05.694
or some Russian
billionaire.


00:33:05.695 --> 00:33:07.564
Keep it down, my kids
are sleeping.


00:33:07.565 --> 00:33:13.098
Get them out of Yellowstone.
It's gonna get ugly here.


00:33:16.318 --> 00:33:18.706
Why don't we
make a baby?


00:33:20.129 --> 00:33:23.054
We're not making a baby
at the supermarket.


00:33:23.955 --> 00:33:27.018
Hands off the
merchandise.


00:33:27.704 --> 00:33:30.198
Honey, woman give me
thousands of dollars


00:33:30.199 --> 00:33:32.567
to handle their boobs.
You get it for free.


00:33:50.660 --> 00:33:53.120
You always act strange
after he shows up.


00:33:53.121 --> 00:33:56.506
I'm not acting strange,
I'm looking for macaroni.


00:33:59.172 --> 00:34:01.021
So why did you stick with
him so long anyways?


00:34:01.022 --> 00:34:02.470
Can we just give
it a rest, please?


00:34:02.471 --> 00:34:05.950
- He's the father of my children.
- Oh, come on, Kate


00:34:05.968 --> 00:34:08.109
You gave up med school so
you could have Noah.


00:34:08.135 --> 00:34:10.241
You practically raised him
and Lilly by yourself


00:34:10.242 --> 00:34:12.380
while he sat glued to a
laptop writing that junk.


00:34:12.381 --> 00:34:14.923
It's not junk!
He's published.


00:34:14.924 --> 00:34:16.515
Oh, published.
Right, I forgot.


00:34:16.516 --> 00:34:19.575
422 copies.


00:34:32.977 --> 00:34:35.673
- Did you see that?
- See what?


00:34:35.691 --> 00:34:38.766
Kate, listen, we have to
keep working at this.


00:34:38.767 --> 00:34:40.229
Our relationship.


00:34:40.690 --> 00:34:43.973
I don't know, Honey, I feel
like there's something


00:34:43.974 --> 00:34:45.460
pulling us apart.


00:34:49.279 --> 00:34:53.809
Grab the pole!
Kate, don't let go!


00:34:56.966 --> 00:34:59.490
Do you have anything
for mosquito bites?


00:34:59.491 --> 00:35:01.412
Before or after?


00:35:02.277 --> 00:35:04.904
- I'll get before and after.
- Stop scratching or you're


00:35:04.905 --> 00:35:06.409
gonna get it all infected.


00:35:06.410 --> 00:35:09.283
<i>...and I had to make a quick
stop at the grocery store...</i>


00:35:09.284 --> 00:35:10.503
It's Mrs Birnbaum


00:35:10.504 --> 00:35:13.658
She's my teacher.
She's on TV!


00:35:14.175 --> 00:35:16.309
<i>...market which was open
for business at the time</i>


00:35:16.310 --> 00:35:19.337
<i>but fortunately there are no
fatalities or injuries reported.</i>


00:35:19.338 --> 00:35:22.412
<i>It really is a miracle
that no one got hurt.</i>


00:35:22.436 --> 00:35:25.131
Hello? Hi mom.


00:35:25.132 --> 00:35:27.811
Did you see what happened
to our supermarket?


00:35:29.730 --> 00:35:32.202
She wants us to
come home.


00:35:32.226 --> 00:35:33.464
Is this even possible?


00:35:33.465 --> 00:35:35.653
We worked every
option through the night.


00:35:35.654 --> 00:35:38.054
The good news: consensus
is that 4 of the Arks


00:35:38.055 --> 00:35:39.794
will be operational in time.


00:35:39.795 --> 00:35:41.606
- Only 4? You call
that good news?


00:35:41.607 --> 00:35:43.838
- We can save over
400.000 people.


00:35:43.839 --> 00:35:45.973
To me, sir, that's nothing
short of a miracle.


00:35:45.974 --> 00:35:48.351
But we have to initiate
the boarding process now.


00:35:48.352 --> 00:35:52.056
Thomas. We don't
have a choice.


00:35:52.105 --> 00:35:55.255
You have got to
convince them.


00:35:58.136 --> 00:36:01.736
According to the
latest information...


00:36:01.749 --> 00:36:04.361
- Please continue, Adrian.
- Thank you, sir.


00:36:04.403 --> 00:36:06.584
The temperature of the
subterranean crust,


00:36:06.585 --> 00:36:10.637
that is the cement that holds
our landmass in place,


00:36:10.638 --> 00:36:13.842
Is increasing at a rapid rate
much faster than anticipated.


00:36:13.853 --> 00:36:16.869
As a result we've observed
extreme polar instability


00:36:16.893 --> 00:36:18.577
The magnetic fields
have decreased


00:36:18.578 --> 00:36:21.353
by more than 80%
in the last 48 hours.


00:36:21.354 --> 00:36:25.010
<i>How much time do we
have, Dr Helmsley?</i>


00:36:26.604 --> 00:36:29.168
Two, maybe three days,
if we're lucky.


00:36:29.202 --> 00:36:32.782
<i>How can you speak about
luck in such a situation?</i>


00:36:32.795 --> 00:36:36.649
Apologies, Mr Prime Minister.


00:36:36.650 --> 00:36:38.563
I meant no disrespect.


00:36:39.004 --> 00:36:41.721
I'm afraid the
longer we wait,


00:36:41.722 --> 00:36:44.114
the more luck
plays its part.


00:36:48.874 --> 00:36:50.849
My friends.


00:36:51.501 --> 00:36:55.046
I recommend we
evacuate immediately.


00:36:56.093 --> 00:36:59.280
If any of you
have objections


00:36:59.639 --> 00:37:02.126
Please speak now.


00:37:02.424 --> 00:37:07.670
<i>In the blue corner:
38 victories, 34 knockouts,</i>


00:37:07.688 --> 00:37:10.437
<i>The fighting machine
from the Ukraine</i>


00:37:10.464 --> 00:37:13.039
<i>The undefeated number
one ranked</i>


00:37:13.040 --> 00:37:14.925
<i>heavyweight challenger:</i>


00:37:14.926 --> 00:37:21.639
<i>Mr. Zultan Balashin!</i>


00:37:25.871 --> 00:37:28.168
- Yuri!
- Zultan!


00:37:28.169 --> 00:37:30.742
I feared you would
not come.


00:37:30.743 --> 00:37:33.047
He needs to concentrate
now. Mr Karpov.


00:37:33.048 --> 00:37:37.063
You shut up while I talk
to my boy, understand?


00:37:37.185 --> 00:37:41.185
- Yes, Mr Karpov.
- Good. That is good.


00:37:41.373 --> 00:37:43.411
Zultan, listen to me.


00:37:43.438 --> 00:37:46.997
We are fighters,
we never go down.


00:37:47.021 --> 00:37:50.923
No matter how
hard they hit us.


00:37:52.329 --> 00:37:57.058
Kill the bastard.


00:37:58.249 --> 00:38:03.998
Let's get ready to rumble!


00:38:20.229 --> 00:38:22.992
ATTENTION:
START BOARDING PROCEDURE


00:38:34.320 --> 00:38:37.197
Yuri, where are you going?


00:38:38.439 --> 00:38:40.230
Yuri!


00:38:48.442 --> 00:38:51.196
<i>CalTech believes that the
fissures running through</i>


00:38:51.197 --> 00:38:54.049
<i>Westwood has released most
of the surface tension.</i>


00:38:54.050 --> 00:38:56.014
<i>Life in the city will
soon return to normal,</i>


00:38:56.015 --> 00:38:56.975
<i>Mayor Gonzales said...</i>


00:38:57.429 --> 00:39:01.356
Okay guys.
Almost home.


00:39:02.158 --> 00:39:03.212
Rise and shine.


00:39:13.414 --> 00:39:15.362
Alright, you're free.


00:39:17.717 --> 00:39:19.442
Mommy!


00:39:20.535 --> 00:39:22.394
Hi, sweetheart.


00:39:26.151 --> 00:39:27.361
Gordon!


00:39:28.585 --> 00:39:30.833
Hey, buddy boy.


00:39:31.545 --> 00:39:32.499
Had a good time?


00:39:33.907 --> 00:39:35.699
God, I missed you.


00:39:36.845 --> 00:39:38.857
- Who wants pancakes?
- Me!


00:39:43.158 --> 00:39:44.996
Thanks for bringing
them home early.


00:39:44.997 --> 00:39:45.957
Yeah.


00:39:47.197 --> 00:39:48.720
Pancakes?


00:39:50.218 --> 00:39:52.087
Late for work.


00:40:02.175 --> 00:40:05.324
- Yes, hello?
- Curtis, where are you?


00:40:05.325 --> 00:40:08.459
- Just back from vacation, sir.
- Good. That is good.


00:40:08.460 --> 00:40:11.520
I will send a jet to pick
up Alec and Oleg.


00:40:11.521 --> 00:40:14.032
Yuri bear. Tell him to bring
the rain coat for Caesar.


00:40:14.033 --> 00:40:15.477
It's in the Range Rover.


00:40:15.478 --> 00:40:16.860
- Curtis?
- Yeah


00:40:16.861 --> 00:40:18.723
Get my boys as
fast as you can.


00:40:18.724 --> 00:40:20.720
I'm hurling towards
you as we speak, sir.


00:40:20.721 --> 00:40:22.490
Good. That is good.


00:40:36.890 --> 00:40:39.826
- Curtis, you're late.
- Good morning to you too.


00:40:44.509 --> 00:40:45.892
Be careful with our stuff.


00:40:45.927 --> 00:40:48.777
Don't get your dirt
on it. Idiot.


00:40:55.192 --> 00:40:57.797
Took you a while,
Mr. Curtis.


00:41:01.050 --> 00:41:04.448
What's your problem?
Be more careful.


00:41:04.449 --> 00:41:05.824
He did that
on purpose.


00:41:05.825 --> 00:41:08.562
Have a safe trip,
you little bastards.


00:41:08.597 --> 00:41:10.090
Now you're
laughing, Curtis.


00:41:10.091 --> 00:41:12.722
But we have tickets
to go on a big ship.


00:41:12.723 --> 00:41:16.145
We will leave,
and you will die.


00:41:27.708 --> 00:41:31.062
<i>Did you hear that?
The authorities in L.A.</i>


00:41:31.063 --> 00:41:33.240
<i>say there's nothing
to worry about.</i>


00:41:33.241 --> 00:41:36.565
<i>I'd love to see their
faces when Malibu</i>


00:41:36.566 --> 00:41:42.083
<i>and Beverly Hills sink
down into the Pacific.</i>


00:41:42.084 --> 00:41:45.388
<i>Where will they plug in
their electric cars then?</i>


00:41:48.846 --> 00:41:49.748
Hey!


00:41:50.173 --> 00:41:51.714
- Is this your plane?
- Yeah


00:41:51.749 --> 00:41:53.255
- Are you a pilot?
- Yeah


00:41:53.256 --> 00:41:54.196
I want to rent it, okay?


00:41:54.231 --> 00:41:55.136
I'll give anything you want.


00:41:55.137 --> 00:41:56.656
Here, take this very
expensive watch.


00:41:56.657 --> 00:41:58.001
My neighbor gave it
to me when he


00:41:58.036 --> 00:41:59.346
thought I was gonna
be somebody.


00:42:03.667 --> 00:42:06.551
<i>...CalTech, that in the
last 36 hours we have</i>


00:42:06.552 --> 00:42:10.182
<i>basically zero earthquake
activity in Southern California,</i>


00:42:10.183 --> 00:42:11.706
<i>which is very rare.</i>


00:42:11.707 --> 00:42:14.681
<i>Unlike the tough characters
I have portrayed in my films...</i>


00:42:14.682 --> 00:42:15.642
Hello?


00:42:16.196 --> 00:42:18.020
Hey. Stop what you're doing.
- Jackson?


00:42:18.021 --> 00:42:20.665
Listen to me. I've rented
a plane, pack up the kids,


00:42:20.666 --> 00:42:22.928
I'm gonna be there
in 5 minutes.


00:42:22.929 --> 00:42:23.742
What are you
talking about?


00:42:23.743 --> 00:42:24.964
We're gonna have
a regular Saturday.


00:42:24.965 --> 00:42:26.649
Noah has music at 2:00
and Lilly has karate.


00:42:26.650 --> 00:42:28.151
You expect him
to remember?


00:42:28.152 --> 00:42:30.529
Kate, California
is going down.


00:42:30.530 --> 00:42:33.592
- Pack up the kids now!
- They just got back.


00:42:33.593 --> 00:42:35.178
God, you sound like
a crazy person.


00:42:35.179 --> 00:42:37.172
The governor just said
we're fine now.


00:42:37.173 --> 00:42:39.726
The guy's an actor, he's
reading a script!


00:42:39.727 --> 00:42:42.052
When they tell you
not to panic


00:42:42.053 --> 00:42:43.955
That's when you run!


00:42:43.956 --> 00:42:47.007
Will you call me back
when you calm down?


00:42:47.099 --> 00:42:49.770
Mommy, why are you
acting so crazy?


00:42:52.222 --> 00:42:53.890
Finish your pancakes,
Al Capone.


00:42:54.429 --> 00:42:58.279
<i>...it seems to me that
the worst is over.</i>


00:43:14.446 --> 00:43:15.174
Hold Mommy's hands!


00:43:20.391 --> 00:43:22.573
Let's go!
- I think it's safer under here!


00:43:22.574 --> 00:43:25.745
Get in the fucking car!


00:43:28.300 --> 00:43:29.434
Come on, kids!


00:43:38.436 --> 00:43:40.923
Get in. Get in.


00:43:40.924 --> 00:43:41.884
My hats!


00:43:47.619 --> 00:43:48.594
Buckle up!


00:43:57.367 --> 00:43:58.575
Sorry.


00:44:11.482 --> 00:44:14.217
Jackson. Hurry up!
Look behind you!


00:44:16.059 --> 00:44:16.947
Oh God.


00:44:22.376 --> 00:44:24.010
Get out of the way!
- Move it!


00:44:24.011 --> 00:44:26.276
Hold on, dear.


00:44:26.277 --> 00:44:27.236
Come on,
you old bags!


00:44:57.618 --> 00:44:59.149
We gotta get to Santa
Monica Airport.


00:44:59.150 --> 00:45:01.342
Take the freeway. It'll
be half the time.


00:45:04.394 --> 00:45:05.393
Yeah, right.


00:45:14.829 --> 00:45:16.900
We gotta get to the other
side of the freeway.


00:45:43.766 --> 00:45:44.449
Dad, look!


00:45:58.951 --> 00:46:01.587
They've just been upgraded
to a 10.9 by Harvard.


00:46:01.588 --> 00:46:03.347
What does CalTech
have to say?


00:46:03.348 --> 00:46:05.526
The city of Pasadena
was wiped out.


00:46:05.527 --> 00:46:07.090
Just a few
minutes ago.


00:46:07.659 --> 00:46:09.468
This is coming in live
from Coachella Valley


00:46:09.469 --> 00:46:11.286
near Joshua Tree.
That huge canyon,


00:46:11.287 --> 00:46:12.528
It wasn't there
this morning.


00:46:13.322 --> 00:46:17.352
100 miles further North,
same thing.


00:46:18.025 --> 00:46:19.656
The San Andreas Fault
is shifting.


00:46:19.945 --> 00:46:20.617
Yes.


00:46:20.618 --> 00:46:23.209
And all major sister
faults in the bay area.


00:46:23.210 --> 00:46:26.282
The whole Pacific Plate
is destabilizing.


00:46:35.689 --> 00:46:36.745
Come on!


00:46:37.033 --> 00:46:39.240
- Who's that?
- Our pilot.


00:46:40.297 --> 00:46:41.544
Dead pilot!


00:46:41.548 --> 00:46:43.272
Gordon!
You can fly!


00:46:43.465 --> 00:46:45.472
I've only had a couple
of lessons in a


00:46:45.473 --> 00:46:47.149
single engine
plane only.


00:46:47.150 --> 00:46:48.841
- You're the guy!
- No, I'm not the guy!


00:46:48.842 --> 00:46:50.036
Trust me!
You're the guy.


00:46:50.037 --> 00:46:52.148
I'm not being
modest about this!


00:46:52.202 --> 00:46:53.415
Come on, kids.


00:46:53.416 --> 00:46:54.806
Gordon's gonna
get us out of here.


00:46:54.807 --> 00:46:57.129
That plane has
multiple engines.


00:46:58.155 --> 00:46:59.498
Jackson!


00:47:14.085 --> 00:47:16.004
- T's and P's
- TNP?


00:47:16.006 --> 00:47:17.541
- What?
- Temperatures and Pressures


00:47:17.542 --> 00:47:18.925
- Let's go!
- My preflight check


00:47:18.926 --> 00:47:20.230
Let him concentrate,
Jackson.


00:47:20.423 --> 00:47:22.054
He has no experience.


00:47:22.151 --> 00:47:23.303
Thank you.


00:47:24.691 --> 00:47:26.662
Gordon! Go!


00:47:26.663 --> 00:47:27.623
Go go go!


00:47:30.695 --> 00:47:32.998
We're not there yet.


00:47:33.958 --> 00:47:36.209
- Punch it!
- We need 85 knots.


00:47:36.210 --> 00:47:37.990
- 80 is good!
- Let's do it.


00:47:44.804 --> 00:47:46.339
Okay, we're up.


00:48:59.011 --> 00:49:01.218
Lilly, go sit with
your brother.


00:49:05.633 --> 00:49:07.744
How did you know
this would happen?


00:49:08.942 --> 00:49:10.720
It's not just California.


00:49:10.912 --> 00:49:13.451
The whole damn world
is going to shit.


00:49:13.696 --> 00:49:16.383
I met this crazy guy
in Yellowstone


00:49:16.384 --> 00:49:18.303
But he's been right about
everything so far


00:49:18.592 --> 00:49:20.586
He said the government
is building these ships,


00:49:20.621 --> 00:49:21.674
space ships,
I don't know what,


00:49:21.708 --> 00:49:23.295
but something...
- Space ships?


00:49:23.584 --> 00:49:25.119
Yeah. Places where
we could be safe.


00:49:25.503 --> 00:49:27.998
He knows where they
are. He's got a map.


00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:31.551
- Jackson...
- Kate, trust me on this.


00:49:31.744 --> 00:49:34.623
Guys. Look.


00:50:02.453 --> 00:50:05.523
<i>But it ain't the end
of the world, Buddy.</i>


00:50:05.716 --> 00:50:08.403
<i>It's only the end
of this song.</i>


00:50:08.595 --> 00:50:12.145
<i>It's been a gas, been a
flip, been a hell of a trip,</i>


00:50:12.147 --> 00:50:16.753
<i>But it ain't the end
of the world.</i>


00:50:17.810 --> 00:50:19.537
Oh yeah!


00:50:19.634 --> 00:50:22.513
- Thank you. Thank you.
- You got fans, Tony.


00:50:24.529 --> 00:50:26.426
There's a call for you, Harry.
Want me to take a message?


00:50:26.449 --> 00:50:28.368
No, thats alright.


00:50:33.648 --> 00:50:34.608
Yeah, hello?


00:50:34.801 --> 00:50:37.008
- Dad?
- Adrian!


00:50:37.201 --> 00:50:40.367
Remember I told you
about that dam in China?


00:50:40.847 --> 00:50:44.302
- Yeah.
- It's happening, Dad.


00:50:53.804 --> 00:50:56.778
They'd probably shoot me
if they knew I told you.


00:50:57.451 --> 00:50:59.279
Nobody's gonna
shoot you, son.


00:50:59.280 --> 00:51:00.240
They need you.


00:51:00.619 --> 00:51:02.118
The President has
ordered us to


00:51:02.119 --> 00:51:03.846
clear out the
White House.


00:51:04.344 --> 00:51:06.985
About time somebody
cleaned up that mess.


00:51:09.765 --> 00:51:11.574
Where are you, Dad?


00:51:11.792 --> 00:51:14.850
What is the course of
The Genesis right now?


00:51:14.858 --> 00:51:17.482
It's all good, Adrian.


00:51:17.483 --> 00:51:20.268
Don't you be worrying
about your old man.


00:51:20.537 --> 00:51:23.428
You have more important
things to do now.


00:51:25.591 --> 00:51:27.147
You know...


00:51:27.916 --> 00:51:30.219
Your mom and I...


00:51:30.493 --> 00:51:33.259
We had one hell of
a great life, son.


00:51:34.897 --> 00:51:38.181
And the best
part about that...


00:51:39.244 --> 00:51:42.843
We had one hell of
a great kid, too.


00:51:47.454 --> 00:51:51.238
This Genesis is a pretty
big ship, son.


00:51:51.432 --> 00:51:55.558
Don't you write your
old man off just yet.


00:51:55.847 --> 00:51:57.382
Besides...


00:51:58.051 --> 00:52:01.202
You know I couldn't
leave Tony alone.


00:52:01.321 --> 00:52:05.654
That old fool can't keep
decent time by himself.


00:52:07.107 --> 00:52:09.199
I love you, Dad.


00:52:14.425 --> 00:52:18.782
I love you too, son.
God knows I do.


00:52:31.162 --> 00:52:34.233
Herb. I want a double.


00:52:34.868 --> 00:52:37.218
- Harry...
- I need a double.


00:52:41.545 --> 00:52:43.379
Thank you, son.


00:52:46.204 --> 00:52:48.513
After 25 year on
the wagon.


00:52:48.514 --> 00:52:50.406
Are you out
of your mind?


00:53:05.824 --> 00:53:07.123
- What are you doing?
- Gotta go.


00:53:07.124 --> 00:53:08.589
That's against
regulation!


00:53:14.079 --> 00:53:15.134
Anything?


00:53:15.235 --> 00:53:16.507
Yeah, there's fuel.
Fill her up, I'm gonna


00:53:16.514 --> 00:53:17.493
gonna go find Charlie.


00:53:17.494 --> 00:53:19.303
Daddy, wait, I wanna
come with you!


00:53:19.304 --> 00:53:20.838
No Lil! No!


00:53:20.839 --> 00:53:22.223
It's alright, I'll take her.
Just fill it up


00:53:22.224 --> 00:53:23.180
I'll be right back.


00:53:23.185 --> 00:53:24.398
Jackson, hurry please!


00:53:25.039 --> 00:53:27.866
<i>I'm standing here at
the highest point</i>


00:53:27.886 --> 00:53:29.666
<i>of what is the rim
of the worlds</i>


00:53:29.667 --> 00:53:34.110
<i>largest super volcano,
Mount Big Horn.</i>


00:53:34.143 --> 00:53:36.535
Charlie!


00:53:39.396 --> 00:53:40.952
<i>I can only hope</i>


00:53:41.144 --> 00:53:43.735
<i>that all of you have
made your peace</i>


00:53:43.875 --> 00:53:44.983
It's gotta be around
here somewhere.


00:53:44.984 --> 00:53:46.791
- Let's go back, Daddy.
- No no no


00:53:46.792 --> 00:53:48.936
We gotta find Charlie,
cause he's got a map.


00:53:48.971 --> 00:53:51.081
It's like a secret map.
Like in pirate movies.


00:53:51.082 --> 00:53:52.404
We gotta work
as a team, okay?


00:53:52.405 --> 00:53:54.326
- Okay
- Okay, come on.


00:53:54.831 --> 00:53:57.493
Call Mom. Tell her we're
gonna be 5 minutes late.


00:54:01.956 --> 00:54:04.355
- Noah.
- I need to talk to Mom.


00:54:04.356 --> 00:54:06.572
- It's Lilly.
- Sweety, where are you?


00:54:06.765 --> 00:54:09.295
- Hi Mommy
- Let me speak to Daddy


00:54:09.433 --> 00:54:12.202
He cant talk right now.
He's driving really fast.


00:54:13.563 --> 00:54:16.713
- Ouch!
- Lilly?


00:54:16.714 --> 00:54:18.537
Who is that? Who's
speaking in the car?


00:54:18.538 --> 00:54:19.912
He's not in the car,
he's on a mountain


00:54:19.913 --> 00:54:21.353
waiting for fireworks.


00:54:21.786 --> 00:54:23.291
Fireworks?
What fireworks?


00:54:23.292 --> 00:54:25.113
Daddy, over there.


00:54:27.445 --> 00:54:28.806
Good job, Lilly.


00:54:30.840 --> 00:54:32.165
Let me talk
to mom now.


00:54:32.262 --> 00:54:35.768
- Hey! We got him.
- Bring back my child!


00:54:40.069 --> 00:54:41.379
You stay here.


00:54:41.380 --> 00:54:43.774
I will go talk to
the pirate, okay?


00:54:52.051 --> 00:54:53.107
Charlie!


00:54:54.800 --> 00:54:55.759
Charlie!


00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:58.446
What are you doing?
I thought you were toast.


00:54:58.481 --> 00:55:00.184
No no no! Where are
the space ships?


00:55:00.405 --> 00:55:02.272
No way you can
make it there.


00:55:02.288 --> 00:55:03.769
We have a plane.
You can come with us.


00:55:03.770 --> 00:55:05.606
But we gotta leave
right now!


00:55:13.490 --> 00:55:16.366
Fly birdies!


00:55:18.499 --> 00:55:19.682
Is this your kid?


00:55:20.945 --> 00:55:22.653
Where's the
god damn map?


00:55:24.738 --> 00:55:25.955
Where's the map?


00:55:27.194 --> 00:55:29.393
- It's in the camper.
- Where in the camper?


00:55:29.421 --> 00:55:32.560
Map section. On the
conspiracy shelf.


00:55:32.561 --> 00:55:33.520
Dewey Decimal System.


00:55:34.257 --> 00:55:36.954
Between Roswell...


00:55:37.051 --> 00:55:40.217
and Marilyn Monroe?


00:55:48.147 --> 00:55:49.813
It's starting.


00:55:57.682 --> 00:55:59.793
You sure you don't
wanna come with me?


00:56:00.189 --> 00:56:03.656
So beautiful,
I'm gonna stay.


00:56:04.453 --> 00:56:05.753
Good luck.


00:56:08.825 --> 00:56:10.510
This marks


00:56:10.511 --> 00:56:15.177
The last day of the
United States of America


00:56:15.447 --> 00:56:20.627
Final hour of all mankind.
As we will be visible from


00:56:20.628 --> 00:56:24.481
the Milky Way as a tiny
little puff of smoke.


00:56:24.735 --> 00:56:29.268
I'm watching the Earth
crumble before my eyes.


00:56:30.133 --> 00:56:32.387
The giant ash cloud


00:56:32.388 --> 00:56:35.252
created by this
super volcano


00:56:35.253 --> 00:56:38.123
will first envelop Vegas,


00:56:38.124 --> 00:56:39.881
and then St. Louis


00:56:39.971 --> 00:56:41.711
and then Chicago,


00:56:41.808 --> 00:56:44.099
and then at long last,


00:56:44.100 --> 00:56:48.509
Washington D.C. will
have its lights go out.


00:56:48.510 --> 00:56:50.259
That guy is crazy,
right Daddy?


00:56:50.260 --> 00:56:51.614
Don't think so.


00:56:54.217 --> 00:56:55.934
This is ridiculous.


00:56:56.017 --> 00:56:57.583
It's been over
half an hour.


00:56:57.669 --> 00:56:59.929
- The guy is a nut job.
- Stop it.


00:57:00.141 --> 00:57:01.850
Noah, give me
the phone again.


00:57:23.098 --> 00:57:25.832
Daddy. What was that?


00:57:26.094 --> 00:57:28.409
Nothing. Nothing.


00:57:28.794 --> 00:57:31.769
I have goosebumps,
people!


00:57:53.002 --> 00:57:55.648
I wish you could see
what I'm seeing, people.


00:57:55.649 --> 00:57:58.623
I wish you could be
here with me!


00:57:58.912 --> 00:58:00.735
Oh, baby!


00:58:02.088 --> 00:58:04.288
Bring it on!


00:58:04.289 --> 00:58:06.595
Always remember folks:


00:58:06.616 --> 00:58:11.679
You heard it first
from Charlie!


00:58:24.719 --> 00:58:28.042
Daddy, it's following us!


00:58:28.072 --> 00:58:29.109
Get down on the
ground and hold on.


00:58:29.110 --> 00:58:31.940
Don't look back.
Just look at me.


00:58:31.941 --> 00:58:34.195
- Do I look scared?
- Uhum.


00:58:38.186 --> 00:58:40.960
Hold on baby.
Hold on tight.


00:58:47.062 --> 00:58:48.947
Daddy, we're on fire!


00:58:56.783 --> 00:58:59.492
There they are!


00:59:04.020 --> 00:59:07.925
It's them.
It's them!


00:59:08.794 --> 00:59:10.744
Mommy!


00:59:13.082 --> 00:59:15.289
Shit.


00:59:20.754 --> 00:59:24.068
Hang on baby.
Hang on


00:59:37.145 --> 00:59:40.148
Mommy.


00:59:46.100 --> 00:59:48.560
- Lil, grab my hand.
- Come on, Noah.


00:59:48.575 --> 00:59:49.711
Lilly, you okay?


00:59:53.911 --> 00:59:57.240
Everybody on? Ready?
- Jackson!


00:59:59.515 --> 01:00:01.774
Where is he?
What's he doing?


01:00:05.272 --> 01:00:06.237
No!


01:00:14.635 --> 01:00:17.850
- Daddy!
- No!


01:00:21.011 --> 01:00:23.120
Hey. We have to go.


01:00:23.121 --> 01:00:24.463
No, we're not
going anywhere!


01:00:24.464 --> 01:00:25.670
Kids, buckle up.
We're leaving.


01:00:25.671 --> 01:00:28.610
He's my dad.
We're gonna wait!


01:00:32.948 --> 01:00:34.402
No!


01:00:34.679 --> 01:00:36.830
Daddy!


01:00:39.807 --> 01:00:44.279
Wait! Wait. Roland,
I see something.


01:00:48.428 --> 01:00:51.135
It's Daddy!


01:00:53.897 --> 01:00:55.570
Slow down!


01:00:55.591 --> 01:00:57.243
Jackson, come on!


01:01:00.431 --> 01:01:01.529
Grab!


01:01:02.662 --> 01:01:04.076
We're running out
of runway.


01:01:04.077 --> 01:01:05.036
For God's sakes, Kate,
pull him up.


01:01:05.990 --> 01:01:07.829
Reach for my hand!


01:01:07.830 --> 01:01:11.242
- Come on!
- Daddy!


01:01:14.809 --> 01:01:17.328
Right. Here we go!


01:01:18.219 --> 01:01:20.517
Faster. Faster.


01:01:38.591 --> 01:01:40.310
Hang on


01:01:42.376 --> 01:01:45.761
- Go faster!
- I'm trying!


01:02:01.148 --> 01:02:05.702
Okay. We're good.
We're good.


01:02:09.248 --> 01:02:11.646
So. Now that you
got your map,


01:02:11.647 --> 01:02:13.194
where are we going?


01:02:18.584 --> 01:02:20.701
CHINA


01:02:23.112 --> 01:02:26.462
We're gonna need
a bigger plane.


01:02:32.156 --> 01:02:34.932
You just said that, Mom.
You just said that.


01:02:34.952 --> 01:02:36.993
You don't remember that
you just said that?


01:02:37.008 --> 01:02:39.995
That's okay.


01:02:40.013 --> 01:02:44.492
Listen, Mom. I'll call you
next week, same time.


01:02:44.513 --> 01:02:49.544
Okay? Take care now.
Take care of yourself.


01:02:51.539 --> 01:02:56.247
Sir. I think you
need to see this.


01:03:00.732 --> 01:03:03.643
I thought they'd give
you an extra ticket, Sir.


01:03:03.644 --> 01:03:04.603
They did.


01:03:04.862 --> 01:03:09.081
But my mother is almost 89.
She's in a wheelchair.


01:03:09.099 --> 01:03:11.627
And she is easily confused.
And I am confident


01:03:11.656 --> 01:03:13.275
that she'll want to
meet her maker


01:03:13.276 --> 01:03:16.291
- on her own terms. Okay?
- Yes, sir.


01:03:16.543 --> 01:03:18.542
- Who are you bringing?
- Nobody.


01:03:18.847 --> 01:03:21.868
My ex-wife said she never
wanted to see me again.


01:03:21.869 --> 01:03:22.991
So be it.


01:03:22.992 --> 01:03:25.110
We could bring people
that contribute.


01:03:26.271 --> 01:03:28.930
<i>...has been damaged by a
series of major earthquakes.</i>


01:03:28.957 --> 01:03:32.382
<i>The death toll is expected to be
well over 2 million people.</i>


01:03:32.413 --> 01:03:35.635
<i>The devastation in Rio de Janeiro
is beyond imagination.</i>


01:03:35.672 --> 01:03:41.088
<i>Two 8.5 tremors have left the people
in the street fighting for resources.</i>


01:03:41.124 --> 01:03:45.237
<i>In the last hour we received this
video from Globo News, Brazil.</i>


01:03:45.741 --> 01:03:48.405
<i>What's happening? My God!</i>


01:03:48.426 --> 01:03:51.758
<i>The statue of Christ is collapsing!</i>


01:03:51.782 --> 01:03:53.918
<i>Fear and chaos have spread
throughout the globe.</i>


01:03:53.953 --> 01:03:57.625
<i>As in London, where the 30th
Olympic Games has been suspended.</i>


01:03:57.654 --> 01:04:00.057
<i>Hundreds of thousands are marching
towards 10 Downing Street</i>


01:04:00.086 --> 01:04:03.458
<i>demanding a lift of the information
blackout proposed by the Prime Minister.</i>


01:04:03.497 --> 01:04:05.892
Thousands of calls to the switchboard.
We had to shut it down.


01:04:05.910 --> 01:04:08.513
<i>We're receiving reports
from all across the globe.</i>


01:04:08.636 --> 01:04:12.917
<i>Millions of distraught masses are
gathering in public places everywhere,</i>


01:04:12.918 --> 01:04:14.393
<i>converging in
desperate prayer.</i>


01:04:14.394 --> 01:04:17.665
<i>Preachers of many faiths
have taken their message of</i>


01:04:17.666 --> 01:04:20.151
<i>the end of the world to
the streets all over the U.S.</i>


01:04:20.152 --> 01:04:22.427
<i>Repent.
There is still time.</i>


01:04:22.440 --> 01:04:24.574
Kind of gaulling when
you realize the nutbags


01:04:24.575 --> 01:04:26.648
with the cardboard signs
had it right the whole time.


01:04:26.649 --> 01:04:29.008
All these people
out there, sir.


01:04:29.009 --> 01:04:30.545
Shouldn't we be issuing
warnings now?


01:04:30.546 --> 01:04:32.770
Only when the boarding
process is complete.


01:04:32.771 --> 01:04:33.583
That's the plan.


01:04:33.584 --> 01:04:36.300
British Columbia
2010, remember?


01:04:36.540 --> 01:04:38.751
Sir, those plans were
drawn up 2 years ago.


01:04:38.754 --> 01:04:44.263
Okay, everybody out.
Come on, get out.


01:04:44.290 --> 01:04:46.380
Wasn't it also decided that
people have the right to


01:04:46.381 --> 01:04:48.487
fight for their lives,
best way they can?


01:04:48.488 --> 01:04:50.928
After we get everyone
on board, Adrian.


01:04:50.929 --> 01:04:52.713
I think that's wrong.


01:04:53.171 --> 01:04:56.208
Want to tell everyone
they're doomed?


01:04:56.243 --> 01:04:57.728
There'd be anarchy.


01:04:57.761 --> 01:05:00.072
You want to jeopardize the
departure of the president?


01:05:00.090 --> 01:05:05.531
Our mission is to assure the
continuity of our species.


01:05:05.576 --> 01:05:08.789
My question:
Can I count on you?


01:05:08.837 --> 01:05:10.999
Can I?


01:05:11.039 --> 01:05:12.228
What?


01:05:12.229 --> 01:05:14.217
The Yellowstone Caldera
has erupted, sir.


01:05:14.218 --> 01:05:17.849
The ash cloud will reach
Washington in 7 hours.


01:05:18.194 --> 01:05:20.872
We've got to get away.


01:05:21.233 --> 01:05:22.506
Where is the
president, Sally?


01:05:22.507 --> 01:05:24.238
Said he wanted to spend
some time alone.


01:05:24.239 --> 01:05:27.058
- I think he's at the chapel.
- He's going to church now?


01:05:27.076 --> 01:05:32.569
He's praying, sir. Which is
not such a bad idea.


01:05:34.145 --> 01:05:36.391
Mr. President. I need
to get you on


01:05:36.392 --> 01:05:38.980
Air Force One
immediately.


01:05:40.531 --> 01:05:41.784
Give me a moment
with Adrian.


01:05:41.793 --> 01:05:43.997
No disrespect sir, we
do not have time.


01:05:44.021 --> 01:05:47.329
Make time.


01:05:57.310 --> 01:06:00.411
Did you ever meet
my wife: Dorothy?


01:06:00.454 --> 01:06:04.236
No sir, I never had
that honor.


01:06:04.324 --> 01:06:08.080
She was in and out
towards the end


01:06:08.086 --> 01:06:10.235
The night before she
passed on, she took


01:06:10.236 --> 01:06:12.083
my hand and told me:


01:06:12.084 --> 01:06:16.455
"I think you should
have a lottery"


01:06:16.491 --> 01:06:21.373
"Everyone should have
a chance to go"


01:06:22.436 --> 01:06:26.512
Maybe that's what we
should have done.


01:06:27.376 --> 01:06:32.303
I'll be the last president of
the United States of America.


01:06:32.346 --> 01:06:35.222
Do you know how
that feels, son?


01:06:35.381 --> 01:06:39.327
No one could have saved
the country, sir.


01:06:39.578 --> 01:06:44.560
And I think, I think people
have a right to know.


01:06:44.733 --> 01:06:48.255
Don't worry, I'll
take care of that.


01:06:48.789 --> 01:06:51.738
Go on now.


01:06:52.000 --> 01:06:54.235
Not without you, sir.


01:06:56.002 --> 01:06:58.145
Get on that plane, son.


01:06:58.161 --> 01:07:01.527
It's a brave new world
you head into


01:07:01.546 --> 01:07:07.123
And a young scientist will
be worth 20 old politicians.


01:07:24.216 --> 01:07:26.516
We should go to my parents
house in the Rockies.


01:07:26.517 --> 01:07:29.382
This isn't one of your crazy
stories, now. Right, Jackson?


01:07:29.383 --> 01:07:30.658
How the hell are we going
to make it to China?


01:07:30.659 --> 01:07:31.692
Hey, Gordon.


01:07:31.693 --> 01:07:33.876
Without Jackson we wouldn't
have made it out of California.


01:07:33.924 --> 01:07:36.266
Noah, please.


01:07:43.451 --> 01:07:45.351
Be careful with
the landing gear!


01:07:45.371 --> 01:07:47.504
Easy gringo, I know
what I'm doing.


01:07:47.505 --> 01:07:48.475
<i>Attention!</i>


01:07:48.476 --> 01:07:50.484
<i>The National Guard
has informed us that an</i>


01:07:50.485 --> 01:07:52.581
<i>extremely hazardous
ash cloud is headed for</i>


01:07:52.582 --> 01:07:53.638
<i>the city of Las Vegas.</i>


01:07:53.639 --> 01:07:55.348
Where are you going?


01:07:57.427 --> 01:07:58.849
Move! You can't
stay here.


01:07:58.850 --> 01:08:01.320
- I have a plane here.
- It's not safe.


01:08:11.587 --> 01:08:15.113
So you got positive
confirmation on this?


01:08:15.419 --> 01:08:18.336
Thank you,
I understand.


01:08:27.378 --> 01:08:30.344
The President
is not coming.


01:08:34.053 --> 01:08:39.809
So, the Captain won't
abandon his sinking ship.


01:08:40.026 --> 01:08:43.423
That's his choice,
and a noble one.


01:08:43.446 --> 01:08:45.242
I have also
just learned


01:08:45.243 --> 01:08:47.398
that the Vice
President's chopper


01:08:47.399 --> 01:08:50.823
went down in the ash
cloud outside Pittsburgh.


01:08:51.032 --> 01:08:54.896
Fortunately, we have
protocols to follow.


01:08:54.914 --> 01:08:56.285
What about the Speaker
of the House?


01:08:56.286 --> 01:08:57.902
In this chaos, I have
no idea. Where is he?


01:08:57.903 --> 01:08:59.489
He's the Commander
in Chief now, sir.


01:08:59.490 --> 01:09:03.097
This is one flight he
shouldn't be late for.


01:09:03.110 --> 01:09:04.400
Tell the Captain
we're taking off.


01:09:04.401 --> 01:09:06.212
Sir, you don't have
the authority.


01:09:06.213 --> 01:09:08.399
Who got the authority?
You? You got the authority?


01:09:08.400 --> 01:09:10.268
You couldn't even keep
your damn mouth shut.


01:09:10.269 --> 01:09:12.714
You betrayed top secret
information.


01:09:12.730 --> 01:09:13.884
What the hell are
you talking about?


01:09:13.885 --> 01:09:15.429
You told your father
everything,


01:09:15.430 --> 01:09:16.889
put this entire
plan in jeopardy,


01:09:16.890 --> 01:09:18.362
Good thing for you
the old man could


01:09:18.397 --> 01:09:19.835
keep his mouth shut
better than you.


01:09:19.836 --> 01:09:21.367
Don't look so shocked.


01:09:21.368 --> 01:09:22.844
We had to monitor
everybody who knew,


01:09:22.845 --> 01:09:24.655
How do you think we kept
it a secret for so long?


01:09:24.656 --> 01:09:27.258
So you just killed anybody
who tried to talk?


01:09:27.289 --> 01:09:29.836
Anybody who tried to talk
was not just an enemy


01:09:29.837 --> 01:09:31.758
of the state. They were
an enemy of humanity.


01:09:31.759 --> 01:09:33.987
The director of the Louvre
was an enemy of humanity?


01:09:33.988 --> 01:09:36.665
After he called a press
conference he was.


01:09:37.160 --> 01:09:39.151
Jesus, what did
you think?


01:09:39.152 --> 01:09:40.323
We're all just gonna
get on board,


01:09:40.324 --> 01:09:42.338
hold hands and
sing Kumbaya?


01:09:43.197 --> 01:09:46.352
Sit down and
buckle up.


01:09:54.203 --> 01:09:57.105
Excuse me, is my father
in the Command Center?


01:09:57.128 --> 01:10:00.125
President is on
the line, Dr Wilson.


01:10:00.558 --> 01:10:03.134
Thank you.


01:10:08.414 --> 01:10:09.667
Where are you?


01:10:09.710 --> 01:10:14.017
You never would've gotten
on that plane if I told you.


01:10:15.423 --> 01:10:17.467
But you said that
you'd be here


01:10:17.468 --> 01:10:19.019
Darling, listen to me.


01:10:19.033 --> 01:10:21.799
Do you understand how
much strength it gives me


01:10:21.800 --> 01:10:24.346
knowing that you
will survive?


01:10:24.990 --> 01:10:28.443
The only thing left
to do now,


01:10:28.464 --> 01:10:31.612
is tell the truth
to people.


01:10:31.647 --> 01:10:36.235
At least if they know,


01:10:36.236 --> 01:10:40.074
families can say
goodbye to each other.


01:10:40.109 --> 01:10:44.275
A mother can comfort
her children.


01:10:45.322 --> 01:10:49.157
And a father...


01:10:49.158 --> 01:10:52.656
can ask his daughter
for forgiveness.


01:11:00.470 --> 01:11:03.857
Whenever you're ready,
Mr President.


01:11:10.702 --> 01:11:13.469
My fellow Americans


01:11:13.698 --> 01:11:17.340
This will be the last
time I address you.


01:11:17.579 --> 01:11:22.984
As you know, catastrophe
has struck our nation.


01:11:23.867 --> 01:11:26.267
Has struck the world.


01:11:26.268 --> 01:11:28.437
I wish I could tell you


01:11:28.438 --> 01:11:31.679
we could prevent
the coming destruction.


01:11:31.695 --> 01:11:33.492
We cannot.


01:11:33.840 --> 01:11:37.376
Today, none of us
are strangers.


01:11:37.619 --> 01:11:40.849
Today, we are
one family,


01:11:40.867 --> 01:11:44.179
stepping into the
darkness together.


01:11:44.202 --> 01:11:47.243
We are a nation of
many religions,


01:11:47.268 --> 01:11:51.135
but I believe these
words reflect the spirit


01:11:51.136 --> 01:11:53.412
of all our faiths:


01:11:53.662 --> 01:11:56.488
"The lord is my
Shepard. I shall... "


01:11:58.307 --> 01:12:01.641
People! Get away from
the doors and windows.


01:12:01.881 --> 01:12:04.282
What are we gonna do?
You tell me.


01:12:04.317 --> 01:12:07.125
- Dr Silberman?
- Tamara!


01:12:07.126 --> 01:12:09.343
What are you
doing here?


01:12:09.344 --> 01:12:10.611
She's a patient,
Honey.


01:12:10.629 --> 01:12:14.078
Excuse me, I have a
private plane out there.


01:12:14.079 --> 01:12:17.196
Karpov! Yuri!


01:12:17.197 --> 01:12:19.349
You knew. This whole
time you knew.


01:12:19.384 --> 01:12:21.822
You've got a way out of here,
right? You got a plane?


01:12:21.845 --> 01:12:24.350
My family, take us
with you. Please!


01:12:24.369 --> 01:12:26.638
Boss, boss.


01:12:26.639 --> 01:12:28.409
I found us a plane.
An Antonov.


01:12:28.410 --> 01:12:29.668
They were just
about to take off,


01:12:29.669 --> 01:12:31.147
but the tower
didn't let them.


01:12:31.148 --> 01:12:34.287
Can you still fly
that thing?


01:12:34.322 --> 01:12:37.426
Sure, Boss, but
I need co-pilot.


01:12:37.447 --> 01:12:40.256
Gordon's a pilot.


01:12:40.257 --> 01:12:42.071
No, I'm not.


01:12:42.072 --> 01:12:44.741
Yes he is. Great pilot.
Let's go.


01:12:44.756 --> 01:12:47.429
Good. Let's go!


01:12:47.455 --> 01:12:51.507
Jackson, stop
saying I'm a pilot.


01:12:51.534 --> 01:12:54.640
You can't go out there.
Come back!


01:12:58.874 --> 01:13:01.194
Move back, people!


01:13:06.646 --> 01:13:09.162
Wow, that's
a big plane.


01:13:09.558 --> 01:13:12.085
It's Russian.


01:13:12.160 --> 01:13:14.144
Let's move everybody.
Come on!


01:13:18.970 --> 01:13:21.457
- Gordon, where are you?
- Let's go!


01:13:21.481 --> 01:13:24.664
Up here, Gordon.
Hurry up!


01:13:24.852 --> 01:13:27.395
Oh my God.


01:13:34.351 --> 01:13:37.831
- Woah, look at these.
- Las Vegas auto show.


01:13:37.841 --> 01:13:40.954
We had VIP tickets
for this.


01:13:40.975 --> 01:13:42.279
That's fantastic, let's go.


01:13:42.308 --> 01:13:44.134
Check the main bus
for hydraulics,


01:13:44.135 --> 01:13:45.287
I'll balance the tanks.


01:13:45.322 --> 01:13:47.388
What?


01:13:47.879 --> 01:13:50.047
Okay, okay.
I'm trying.


01:13:52.135 --> 01:13:54.126
Tower to Antonov, what
the hell are you doing?


01:13:54.127 --> 01:13:55.086
Shut down immediately.


01:14:02.790 --> 01:14:03.898
- Caesar, shh.


01:14:04.444 --> 01:14:05.481
When I say "go"


01:14:05.482 --> 01:14:07.377
we push all this down
at once, okay?


01:14:07.397 --> 01:14:08.938
- Okay.
- Go!


01:14:08.971 --> 01:14:12.987
Antonov, abort take-off.
You do not have clearance.


01:14:13.025 --> 01:14:16.571
I repeat, you
must abort.


01:14:21.532 --> 01:14:22.676
What the hell
was that?


01:14:22.677 --> 01:14:25.067
I don't know, but
it's not good.


01:14:27.185 --> 01:14:30.319
- Push!
- Pushing! Come on!


01:14:33.414 --> 01:14:35.840
We're going down!


01:14:44.052 --> 01:14:46.331
It must be the...
Take over.


01:14:46.365 --> 01:14:49.178
What do you mean,
take over?


01:14:50.852 --> 01:14:52.864
- Sasha!
- Relax.


01:14:52.894 --> 01:14:54.514
Now!


01:14:58.948 --> 01:14:59.808
Jesus.


01:15:02.721 --> 01:15:04.422
- Oh God
- I think I got it


01:15:04.454 --> 01:15:07.316
- Sasha, now!
- Take a deep breath.


01:15:07.912 --> 01:15:09.302
Pull!


01:15:34.894 --> 01:15:37.332
Was that the Eiffel Tower?


01:15:37.473 --> 01:15:41.165
I think so.


01:15:46.308 --> 01:15:51.999
Ladies and Gentlemen.
We're on our way to China.


01:15:52.318 --> 01:15:57.325
Good. Very good.


01:16:04.752 --> 01:16:06.868
Do not believe in
something simply


01:16:06.869 --> 01:16:09.892
because you have
heard it, Nima.


01:16:09.893 --> 01:16:13.605
But great Lama.
Tenzin is my brother.


01:16:13.661 --> 01:16:15.090
He works inside
the big tunnel,


01:16:15.091 --> 01:16:16.932
where the ships
are built.


01:16:19.328 --> 01:16:22.154
But what is there
in your wisdom,


01:16:22.155 --> 01:16:24.480
great Lama,
if Tenzin is right?


01:16:24.481 --> 01:16:28.687
What if our world is
indeed coming to and end?


01:16:36.453 --> 01:16:39.855
It is full, great Rinpoche.


01:16:45.020 --> 01:16:46.414
Like this cup,


01:16:46.457 --> 01:16:52.214
you are full of opinions and
speculations.


01:16:52.577 --> 01:16:54.561
To see the light
of wisdom,


01:16:54.602 --> 01:16:58.772
You first must
empty your cup.


01:17:14.107 --> 01:17:16.000
Be careful with
the clutch...


01:17:16.361 --> 01:17:18.669
It tends to slip.


01:17:37.350 --> 01:17:39.304
Grandpa, Nima is here!


01:17:39.337 --> 01:17:41.093
Grandma, I got a message
from Tenzin...


01:17:41.127 --> 01:17:43.098
He want us to meet
him in Cho Ming


01:17:43.099 --> 01:17:44.058
at the work camp.


01:17:45.443 --> 01:17:48.044
He says he can get us onto
the ships he's working on.


01:17:48.045 --> 01:17:49.866
What are you
talking about?


01:17:49.867 --> 01:17:52.346
Tenzin works
on the dam.


01:17:54.842 --> 01:17:56.222
Grandma...


01:17:56.867 --> 01:18:00.166
...the dam is a ship.
The government lied to us.


01:18:00.863 --> 01:18:02.723
There will be a big flood!


01:18:03.372 --> 01:18:04.993
We must pack up
right away.


01:18:05.159 --> 01:18:07.927
Nima? Who gave
you a truck?


01:18:08.621 --> 01:18:11.774
We took a trip on the
Liam Song ferry once


01:18:11.898 --> 01:18:14.522
Grandpa threw up
the whole way.


01:18:15.479 --> 01:18:17.346
Let's eat first.


01:18:21.962 --> 01:18:25.482
Hey, look, the new Bentley!
Our father had one on order.


01:18:25.903 --> 01:18:27.814
He was supposed to
get it next year.


01:18:27.815 --> 01:18:30.641
But then he canceled it.
Because of the ships.


01:18:31.314 --> 01:18:33.360
How many cars does
your family have?


01:18:33.394 --> 01:18:36.376
My mom's boyfriend
has a Porsche.


01:18:37.360 --> 01:18:39.531
Our parents are
divorced too.


01:18:41.709 --> 01:18:43.282
Found a hat.


01:18:43.574 --> 01:18:45.597
She has a thing
for hats.


01:18:45.598 --> 01:18:47.874
I was just like
that at her age.


01:18:48.261 --> 01:18:50.157
They made me
feel safe.


01:18:50.766 --> 01:18:54.069
So, how did you meet
Dr Silberman?


01:18:55.062 --> 01:18:57.400
As you can see not the
same way you did.


01:18:58.906 --> 01:19:02.560
My boyfriend asked me
to get them done


01:19:02.702 --> 01:19:04.528
But he's not
your husband?


01:19:04.900 --> 01:19:06.492
We are not married.


01:19:06.493 --> 01:19:08.624
And probably
never will be.


01:19:15.770 --> 01:19:17.625
For the boys.


01:19:21.471 --> 01:19:24.827
They seem to like
each other.


01:19:26.367 --> 01:19:27.932
Yeah, I guess.


01:19:29.158 --> 01:19:32.129
Tell me, Mr Karpov,
how much did you pay?


01:19:32.207 --> 01:19:36.601
One billion Euro.
Per seat.


01:19:37.984 --> 01:19:40.582
That's disgusting
- Oh yeah?


01:19:41.380 --> 01:19:45.357
You know, Curtis, I wasn't
always a businessman.


01:19:45.466 --> 01:19:47.651
I am a boxer.


01:19:47.652 --> 01:19:49.662
Was my only playing
when I was boy


01:19:49.663 --> 01:19:52.646
back in Murmansk.
And my coach,


01:19:52.680 --> 01:19:57.451
his name was also Yuri.
He always said:


01:19:57.486 --> 01:20:00.935
"If someone wants
to beat you...


01:20:00.936 --> 01:20:03.708
...he has to
kill you first"


01:20:06.682 --> 01:20:09.650
That's very nice.


01:20:10.115 --> 01:20:12.705
But tell me, what
would you have done


01:20:12.740 --> 01:20:15.593
if you were rich
like me?


01:20:15.594 --> 01:20:18.728
Look, they are
wonderful children.


01:20:20.123 --> 01:20:23.313
OK guys. The plan is
to refill in Hawaii,


01:20:23.314 --> 01:20:25.460
so sit down and
buckle up.


01:20:25.461 --> 01:20:28.589
Gordon and I
will do the rest.


01:20:29.933 --> 01:20:31.558
Oh God.


01:20:32.966 --> 01:20:34.773
Go get the guys.


01:20:37.172 --> 01:20:42.353
Guys, there's a...
You might wanna...


01:20:58.053 --> 01:21:02.601
- What is that?
- The state of Hawaii


01:21:03.023 --> 01:21:06.983
Not good. That is
not good.


01:21:11.594 --> 01:21:13.379
How much fuel do
we have left?


01:21:13.380 --> 01:21:14.514
Not enough.


01:21:14.515 --> 01:21:16.734
We have to make a
water landing


01:21:16.735 --> 01:21:18.631
Somewhere in
South China sea.


01:21:18.744 --> 01:21:21.773
Great, at least we won't
need a landing gear.


01:21:21.808 --> 01:21:24.803
- What about it?
- We lost it all, in Vegas.


01:21:34.871 --> 01:21:36.924
Dr Wilson,
may I come in?


01:21:37.481 --> 01:21:39.850
I'm not very good
company, I'm afraid.


01:21:40.817 --> 01:21:43.823
- Doctor...
- Please, call me Adrian.


01:21:49.157 --> 01:21:51.585
All those people
we left behind.


01:21:51.952 --> 01:21:54.649
They don't stand
a chance, do they?


01:21:55.798 --> 01:21:58.661
I believe that nature
will choose for itself,


01:21:58.662 --> 01:22:01.746
from itself, what
will survive.


01:22:02.458 --> 01:22:06.228
Just like you, preserving
those great artworks.


01:22:06.362 --> 01:22:08.900
Our culture is our
soul, and that's not


01:22:08.901 --> 01:22:10.388
dying tonight.


01:22:10.389 --> 01:22:14.576
Come on, I contributed
to this cover up.


01:22:14.577 --> 01:22:17.853
The Da Vinci, Picasso,
they're in.


01:22:17.854 --> 01:22:21.036
But if you're some nobody
you don't stand a chance.


01:22:21.711 --> 01:22:24.041
It's not necessarily true.


01:22:24.680 --> 01:22:28.549
Did you ever hear of a writer
called Jackson Curtis?


01:22:28.670 --> 01:22:31.652
Wrote a book,
"Farewell Atlantis".


01:22:31.653 --> 01:22:32.994
What do you think the
chances are of an


01:22:32.995 --> 01:22:35.938
unknown writer who
barely sold 500 copies


01:22:35.939 --> 01:22:38.063
making it aboard
this plane?


01:22:39.100 --> 01:22:41.565
- I don't understand
- I mean call it chance


01:22:41.566 --> 01:22:44.223
or faith or nature,
doesn't matter


01:22:44.224 --> 01:22:48.121
This book is part of our
legacy now. Why?


01:22:48.214 --> 01:22:49.998
Because I'm reading it.


01:22:52.850 --> 01:22:56.746
Dr Helmsley, please report
to the situation room.


01:23:08.982 --> 01:23:10.110
Who is it?


01:23:10.111 --> 01:23:12.983
<i>- Hello, I'm sorry.
Who is this?</i>


01:23:13.191 --> 01:23:15.253
This is Yoko Delgado.


01:23:15.254 --> 01:23:17.903
Do you want to
speak to my daddy?


01:23:20.326 --> 01:23:21.730
Yes, please.


01:23:21.731 --> 01:23:24.199
<i>Who should I
say is calling?</i>


01:23:27.264 --> 01:23:32.468
- Tell him, its his father.
- You're my grandpa?


01:23:32.842 --> 01:23:35.013
Yes, sweetheart, I am.


01:23:37.062 --> 01:23:40.275
Daddy, grandpa
is on the phone.


01:24:40.400 --> 01:24:42.455
Mr President, Sir.


01:24:49.267 --> 01:24:52.498
- What's the matter, sweety?
- She can't find her daddy.


01:24:54.057 --> 01:24:58.992
Why don't you two get
comfy on that couch?


01:25:00.391 --> 01:25:02.499
I'll find your daddy.


01:25:09.588 --> 01:25:11.435
Who can help me with
missing persons?


01:25:11.436 --> 01:25:14.731
Sorry, man, I'm really
busy right now.


01:25:15.260 --> 01:25:18.358
I mean of course, sir.
Sorry, Mr President.


01:25:18.359 --> 01:25:21.359
- Don't worry about it, you're
doing a great job, son.


01:25:45.938 --> 01:25:46.828
What's happening?


01:25:46.829 --> 01:25:48.376
The Capitol has
been hit by a 9.4


01:25:48.377 --> 01:25:49.871
Lost communication with
the White House, sir.


01:25:49.872 --> 01:25:52.731
- Where is it centered?
- North Chesapeake Bay.


01:25:56.311 --> 01:25:59.600
Mr Anheuser, Russian
president on the line, sir.


01:25:59.862 --> 01:26:01.050
Excuse me.


01:26:01.872 --> 01:26:03.901
We just entered
Chinese air space.


01:26:05.438 --> 01:26:07.436
That's affirmative,
Mr President.


01:26:07.437 --> 01:26:10.604
Until communication
is restored,


01:26:10.605 --> 01:26:12.217
I suppose I am
in command.


01:26:12.783 --> 01:26:14.261
It appears that all
other heads of state


01:26:14.262 --> 01:26:16.358
are en route, with the
exception of the


01:26:16.359 --> 01:26:17.319
Italian Prime Minister,


01:26:18.456 --> 01:26:20.983
Who has also
decided to


01:26:21.018 --> 01:26:24.240
stay behind and
trust in prayer.


01:27:26.728 --> 01:27:29.493
Earths crust has begun
to shift, Dr Helmsley!


01:27:29.577 --> 01:27:32.744
- By what degree?
- 1.2°. Still moving.


01:27:32.827 --> 01:27:34.095
So, what happens next?


01:27:34.096 --> 01:27:36.661
The movement of our land
masses comes to a halt.


01:27:36.695 --> 01:27:38.116
Let's see a simulation.


01:27:39.448 --> 01:27:41.361
Expect the formation
of gigantic tsunamis.


01:27:41.362 --> 01:27:44.590
Proportional to the magnitude
of corresponding quakes.


01:27:49.370 --> 01:27:51.175
Pull up the Japanese
sea border.


01:27:51.176 --> 01:27:52.136
Yes, sir.


01:27:53.249 --> 01:27:55.607
My dad's on a cruise
ship out there.


01:27:56.782 --> 01:27:59.207
But I guess you already
knew that.


01:28:00.138 --> 01:28:02.054
Sir, we've recorded
two underwater quakes


01:28:02.055 --> 01:28:04.413
at 7.9 and 8.2.


01:28:20.786 --> 01:28:23.163
From what we have just
learned, Tokyo seems to


01:28:23.198 --> 01:28:25.541
have taken the full
force of the earthquake.


01:28:25.542 --> 01:28:27.649
At this point unconfirmed
reports indicate that


01:28:27.650 --> 01:28:30.632
large areas of land
are under water.


01:28:30.633 --> 01:28:32.056
Please stay tuned
for further...


01:28:41.681 --> 01:28:43.372
Tony


01:28:43.599 --> 01:28:46.181
I called.


01:28:48.352 --> 01:28:50.857
I was too late.


01:28:54.677 --> 01:28:58.258
Maybe they got
out of town.


01:28:58.259 --> 01:28:59.650
You never know.


01:30:23.776 --> 01:30:26.317
I'm coming home,
Dorothy.


01:30:51.832 --> 01:30:53.218
Anything?


01:30:54.126 --> 01:30:56.142
Nothing but static.


01:30:56.143 --> 01:30:57.870
Not even an
emergency signal.


01:31:09.794 --> 01:31:12.828
Can't think about what's
going on down there


01:31:19.858 --> 01:31:21.798
Remember that old Beetle
we used to camp in?


01:31:21.799 --> 01:31:23.430
But you'd never
get the roof up.


01:31:24.615 --> 01:31:28.029
We definitely
traded up.


01:31:30.201 --> 01:31:32.351
Tried to find our old
spot at Yellowstone.


01:31:32.352 --> 01:31:35.032
When I went camping
with the kids, but...


01:31:35.033 --> 01:31:36.885
I couldn't find it.


01:31:46.139 --> 01:31:48.969
Do you think
people change?


01:31:48.970 --> 01:31:50.941
By people, do
you mean me?


01:31:50.942 --> 01:31:51.610
Yes.


01:31:51.611 --> 01:31:54.448
Do you think you've changed
since we separated?


01:31:55.523 --> 01:31:58.097
I seem to eat a lot
more cereal now.


01:32:02.162 --> 01:32:05.021
You always had
tunnel vision.


01:32:05.022 --> 01:32:07.997
You could just block
everything out and write.


01:32:11.389 --> 01:32:13.485
You blocked us out.


01:32:22.020 --> 01:32:23.456
Do you love him?


01:32:26.178 --> 01:32:28.063
I love him enough.


01:32:39.401 --> 01:32:42.669
All global ground communication
is ceased, sir.


01:32:46.369 --> 01:32:51.137
The only signals our
satellites are picking up


01:32:51.755 --> 01:32:54.298
Well there's a piece
of good news.


01:32:54.299 --> 01:32:55.546
Any updates, Doctor?


01:32:55.651 --> 01:32:59.078
We expect the tsunamis to reach
land fall on every continent.


01:32:59.208 --> 01:33:00.882
The Cho Ming area will
be impacted in


01:33:00.917 --> 01:33:02.610
approximately 6 hours.


01:33:03.475 --> 01:33:05.936
It looks like the crust
have shifted by almost


01:33:05.937 --> 01:33:08.178
23 degrees to
the southwest.


01:33:08.839 --> 01:33:11.320
The data also shows
the Earth's poles


01:33:11.321 --> 01:33:13.451
have reversed their
magnetic fields.


01:33:13.452 --> 01:33:15.419
These are their
new positions.


01:33:15.971 --> 01:33:20.894
You're telling me that
the North Pole


01:33:20.895 --> 01:33:23.101
is now somewhere
in Wisconsin?


01:33:23.102 --> 01:33:25.907
Actually, thats the
South Pole now.


01:33:33.815 --> 01:33:36.182
Engine failure.
2 of 6 are down.


01:33:36.183 --> 01:33:37.792
You must get ready.


01:33:38.979 --> 01:33:42.316
- How long do we have?
- 18 minutes. Maybe.


01:33:44.011 --> 01:33:45.585
Better wake
up the kids.


01:33:45.586 --> 01:33:46.859
Da.


01:34:25.059 --> 01:34:26.325
Why do you
hate Gordon?


01:34:30.854 --> 01:34:34.222
Hey. Come on.


01:34:35.088 --> 01:34:39.247
What are you talking about?
I don't hate him.


01:34:39.547 --> 01:34:41.073
You don't like him either


01:34:41.160 --> 01:34:44.147
That's because I don't
know him well, maybe.


01:34:44.290 --> 01:34:45.568
But I do.


01:34:45.569 --> 01:34:47.787
He's really nice once
you get to know him.


01:34:47.822 --> 01:34:49.445
You should talk
to him more often.


01:34:49.446 --> 01:34:52.099
You guys would get
along really well.


01:34:55.179 --> 01:34:57.008
You like him a lot, huh?


01:35:04.760 --> 01:35:08.562
I'll do my best.
I promise. OK?


01:35:09.866 --> 01:35:13.249
I'm really proud of you.
Really proud of you.


01:35:14.704 --> 01:35:16.551
Is it time?


01:35:18.276 --> 01:35:20.324
Yeah


01:35:22.645 --> 01:35:23.976
Dad, what's wrong?


01:35:24.361 --> 01:35:27.120
Sasha's gotta land.
It's gonna be a little bumpy.


01:35:27.121 --> 01:35:28.368
Maybe a little wet.


01:35:29.379 --> 01:35:30.378
Daddy?


01:35:36.183 --> 01:35:38.287
Hold her steady.


01:35:54.382 --> 01:35:58.230
Daddy, I'm not a
really good swimmer.


01:35:58.231 --> 01:35:59.600
Hey, that's alright. It's
what you got this for.


01:36:00.691 --> 01:36:03.165
It's like being in
a swimming pool.


01:36:03.166 --> 01:36:06.791
Only it's got more cool stuff.
It's got a whistle, a light.


01:36:07.942 --> 01:36:09.710
I thought we were
going to China.


01:36:10.486 --> 01:36:12.506
No, we gotta
land here.


01:36:15.410 --> 01:36:16.695
So that's what
we're gonna do.


01:36:16.696 --> 01:36:17.998
We're just gonna
all stay together.


01:36:18.262 --> 01:36:19.498
No we're not,
we're gonna die!


01:36:19.499 --> 01:36:21.537
No, we're not.


01:36:21.665 --> 01:36:23.056
Promise?


01:36:23.174 --> 01:36:24.910
I promise you, we'll
all stay together,


01:36:24.911 --> 01:36:27.066
no matter what happens.


01:36:41.267 --> 01:36:43.827
Jackson, Yuri.


01:36:45.873 --> 01:36:47.288
I think you better
come up here


01:36:48.401 --> 01:36:49.904
I'm gonna go check
this out.


01:36:50.045 --> 01:36:51.020
- Dad, dad!
- I'll be right back


01:36:51.897 --> 01:36:54.702
We gotta buckle
up. Let's go.


01:36:55.913 --> 01:36:58.086
Don't ask me how
that happened


01:36:58.878 --> 01:36:59.957
There is no more
ocean, and we're


01:36:59.958 --> 01:37:01.898
pretty close to where
we wanted to go.


01:37:01.899 --> 01:37:03.958
It's like the whole world
shifted by 1000 miles.


01:37:04.010 --> 01:37:06.672
1578 to be exact.


01:37:06.673 --> 01:37:08.927
It's called "Earth Crust
Displacement Theory"


01:37:08.928 --> 01:37:10.874
Professor Hapgood 1958.


01:37:12.442 --> 01:37:13.656
Way to go, Charlie.


01:37:16.772 --> 01:37:17.689
What was that?


01:37:19.250 --> 01:37:21.660
We just lost our
last two engines.


01:37:39.538 --> 01:37:41.092
I'll shoot for that glacier.


01:37:41.126 --> 01:37:42.380
It's going to
get rocky.


01:37:42.414 --> 01:37:44.297
Listen, it's gonna
sound crazy,


01:37:44.298 --> 01:37:46.397
but here's what
you have to do.


01:37:50.358 --> 01:37:53.591
Get up! Follow me!


01:37:53.835 --> 01:37:55.718
Yuri, what are you doing?


01:37:56.177 --> 01:37:58.275
We are taking the Bentley!


01:37:59.283 --> 01:38:01.727
Not yet!
Not yet.


01:38:03.680 --> 01:38:04.906
Almost there.


01:38:05.884 --> 01:38:07.033
Get in the car.


01:38:17.561 --> 01:38:19.925
Okay, go now!
Pull!


01:38:24.668 --> 01:38:25.651
No no no no no


01:38:30.137 --> 01:38:31.255
Go, Jackson.


01:38:31.256 --> 01:38:33.060
We gotta wait
for Sasha and Gordon.


01:38:34.020 --> 01:38:35.914
Go! Make sure
everybody gets


01:38:35.915 --> 01:38:37.924
off the plane before
I touch down.


01:38:37.925 --> 01:38:39.083
What about you?


01:38:39.117 --> 01:38:42.953
I'll be fine. I have to
touch this plane down.


01:38:44.012 --> 01:38:46.632
What are you
waiting for? Go!


01:39:02.191 --> 01:39:03.727
There he is.
I see him!


01:39:04.001 --> 01:39:05.533
Come on lets go.


01:39:05.534 --> 01:39:07.102
- Where is Sasha?
- He said he's fine


01:39:07.103 --> 01:39:09.509
We should get out of here
before he touches down.


01:39:09.543 --> 01:39:10.814
Don't go!


01:39:11.990 --> 01:39:13.695
Go Jackson, go.


01:39:15.453 --> 01:39:16.542
It wont start.


01:39:17.911 --> 01:39:20.551
Shut up everybody!


01:39:21.889 --> 01:39:23.712
Engine


01:39:23.713 --> 01:39:25.648
Start


01:39:28.399 --> 01:39:31.395
Voice control.
Sold me on it.


01:41:28.860 --> 01:41:31.717
Welcome, to the People's
Republic of China.


01:41:31.718 --> 01:41:33.651
- Good to be here.
- Say hi, kids.


01:41:33.685 --> 01:41:34.796
Hi


01:41:34.829 --> 01:41:37.916
- What color are your passes?
- What?


01:41:37.950 --> 01:41:40.035
What color are your
boarding passes?


01:41:41.834 --> 01:41:44.190
I have green cards.


01:41:44.769 --> 01:41:47.502
- For my boys and me.
- What?


01:41:50.665 --> 01:41:52.561
Yuri? Yuri!


01:41:53.397 --> 01:41:56.385
Yuri. It's a mistake.
A joke, eh?


01:41:57.088 --> 01:42:02.182
What? You think I didn't know
about you and Sasha?


01:42:02.215 --> 01:42:06.781
May God bless that poor
bastard's soul.


01:42:11.669 --> 01:42:15.167
I'm sorry guys.
Good luck.


01:42:15.510 --> 01:42:17.341
Come on, boys.


01:42:18.744 --> 01:42:21.192
Maybe with money
we could bribe them.


01:42:21.226 --> 01:42:22.993
You got a billion Euros?


01:42:27.166 --> 01:42:31.691
Dr Wilson. I'm Captain Michaels,
Skipper of the American ship.


01:42:31.725 --> 01:42:34.145
Please accept my sincere
condolences for your father.


01:42:34.146 --> 01:42:35.490
Thank you, Captain.


01:42:36.983 --> 01:42:40.146
Anheuser. Your party
is the last to arrive.


01:42:44.075 --> 01:42:46.338
There's been reports of
severe damage, Captain.


01:42:46.339 --> 01:42:48.431
What's the status of
Ark number 3?


01:42:48.432 --> 01:42:50.404
We haven't done a
complete assessment yet.


01:42:50.405 --> 01:42:52.611
Looks like we lost it.


01:43:01.476 --> 01:43:04.708
No toothbrush.
Only books.


01:43:04.742 --> 01:43:08.217
When I was a kid my dad
was on the road a lot.


01:43:09.205 --> 01:43:13.316
He'd always leave me
a box full of books.


01:43:13.811 --> 01:43:17.216
I'd get an ice cream cone
for every book I read so...


01:43:17.217 --> 01:43:19.000
I was a fat kid.


01:43:19.281 --> 01:43:21.653
I find that very hard
to believe.


01:43:21.654 --> 01:43:26.524
No, its true, my high school
carrier was 2000 books


01:43:26.525 --> 01:43:28.178
Zero girlfriends.


01:43:29.150 --> 01:43:32.464
I didn't even kiss a boy
until I was in college.


01:43:32.465 --> 01:43:35.067
They were all too
scared of my dad.


01:44:20.787 --> 01:44:22.085
Leave it to the Chinese.


01:44:22.717 --> 01:44:24.118
I didn't think
it was possible.


01:44:24.119 --> 01:44:26.003
Not in the
time we had.


01:44:26.453 --> 01:44:28.365
That's Ark number 3, sir.


01:44:28.852 --> 01:44:30.568
The roof collapsed
during the shifting


01:44:30.569 --> 01:44:31.528
of the Earth's crust.


01:44:33.015 --> 01:44:34.113
Jesus Christ.


01:44:44.026 --> 01:44:45.334
Hey, what's going on here?


01:44:45.369 --> 01:44:47.864
I have a green card for
my boys and me.


01:44:47.865 --> 01:44:50.123
I want to speak to
your supervisor.


01:44:50.124 --> 01:44:51.806
I am the supervisor.


01:44:51.807 --> 01:44:53.193
Get back with the
other green cards,


01:44:53.194 --> 01:44:54.845
or I'll have
you detained.


01:44:56.937 --> 01:44:58.894
What he said about you
and Sasha, is it true?


01:44:58.895 --> 01:45:03.006
Sasha was worth a hundred
times a man like Yuri.


01:45:03.007 --> 01:45:04.945
I should have listened
to you, Dr. Silberman.


01:45:04.946 --> 01:45:07.786
I actually liked the way
I looked before that


01:45:07.787 --> 01:45:10.200
monster talked
me into it.


01:45:10.201 --> 01:45:12.403
Did you know he asked
me for a discount?


01:45:12.404 --> 01:45:14.344
He payed in installments.


01:45:14.345 --> 01:45:15.765
Cheap bastard.


01:45:16.444 --> 01:45:17.666
You hear that?


01:45:20.221 --> 01:45:21.735
Over there!


01:45:25.113 --> 01:45:27.250
Stop!


01:45:33.147 --> 01:45:36.441
Stop!


01:46:07.566 --> 01:46:09.030
How were all these
people chosen?


01:46:09.031 --> 01:46:10.347
Same way your Arc was.


01:46:10.348 --> 01:46:11.413
By experts from all
over the world.


01:46:11.448 --> 01:46:13.252
We had geneticists
determine the perfect


01:46:13.253 --> 01:46:14.877
gene pool we need
to repopulate.


01:46:14.878 --> 01:46:16.566
These people were chosen
by geneticists?


01:46:16.567 --> 01:46:18.518
<i>All green card holders</i>


01:46:18.519 --> 01:46:20.261
<i>Please proceed to
hangar D-4</i>


01:46:20.262 --> 01:46:22.197
Looks to me like their check
books got them on board.


01:46:22.232 --> 01:46:24.132
That's right, Dr Wilson.
Without billions of dollars


01:46:24.167 --> 01:46:26.271
from the private sector
this entire operation


01:46:26.272 --> 01:46:27.232
would've been
impossible.


01:46:27.488 --> 01:46:28.693
We sold tickets?


01:46:29.619 --> 01:46:30.630
What about all
these workers?


01:46:31.391 --> 01:46:32.685
They all get passes?


01:46:33.209 --> 01:46:35.629
What? Life isn't fair?


01:46:35.904 --> 01:46:36.660
Is that it?


01:46:37.081 --> 01:46:38.499
If you want to
donate your passes,


01:46:38.500 --> 01:46:41.803
to a couple of Chinese
workers, be my guest.


01:46:42.463 --> 01:46:43.829
Captain, I want a
pre-launch briefing.


01:46:43.830 --> 01:46:45.673
All international
teams present.


01:47:19.357 --> 01:47:21.162
What the hell?


01:47:24.236 --> 01:47:27.119
What is this? They could've
fit 10 people in here.


01:47:33.922 --> 01:47:35.243
Satnam, where are you?


01:47:35.793 --> 01:47:38.394
- On the Nampan Plateau.
- What?


01:47:40.252 --> 01:47:42.613
There's a tidal wave
coming from the east.


01:47:42.614 --> 01:47:43.765
It's gigantic.


01:47:44.133 --> 01:47:45.676
<i>Satnam, what
happened?</i>


01:47:45.677 --> 01:47:47.470
We never got
picked up, Adrian.


01:47:47.471 --> 01:47:49.658
The airlift
never came.


01:47:51.448 --> 01:47:52.859
Goodbye, my friend.


01:47:53.891 --> 01:47:56.558
Satnam


01:48:21.771 --> 01:48:23.938
- Where are we set up?
- Over there.


01:48:28.554 --> 01:48:31.242
Give me the satellite
images from Napam, India.


01:48:31.655 --> 01:48:32.307
What's happening?


01:48:33.478 --> 01:48:36.078
Satnam was talking
about another wave,


01:48:36.079 --> 01:48:37.614
coming from the east.


01:48:41.059 --> 01:48:42.325
- Holy mother of God.


01:48:42.326 --> 01:48:44.596
So the flooding
will hit earlier?


01:48:44.597 --> 01:48:46.303
The second wave
is closer?


01:48:46.304 --> 01:48:47.382
Plug in the new data.


01:48:49.152 --> 01:48:50.707
Satnam didn't
get picked up.


01:48:50.708 --> 01:48:51.667
What?


01:48:51.887 --> 01:48:54.413
A lot of people didn't get
picked up in this chaos.


01:48:54.723 --> 01:48:56.731
This is not a conspiracy,
Helmsley.


01:48:56.732 --> 01:48:58.045
Your predictions haven't
exactly panned out,


01:48:58.046 --> 01:48:59.603
have they, Doctor?


01:48:59.604 --> 01:49:01.837
It's ready.


01:49:03.422 --> 01:49:05.640
Oh God, its 1500
meters high.


01:49:06.717 --> 01:49:08.114
When will it
get here?


01:49:08.649 --> 01:49:09.728
Talk to me, Hemsley,
when will it hit?


01:49:09.729 --> 01:49:11.886
Adjust the countdown.


01:49:27.069 --> 01:49:30.256
28 minutes, 10 seconds
to impact.


01:49:30.257 --> 01:49:31.035
My God.


01:49:31.437 --> 01:49:33.236
Captain.


01:49:33.237 --> 01:49:35.083
I need to speak to the
other heads of state.


01:49:35.084 --> 01:49:36.493
- Right away. Taylor?
- Aye, Captain


01:49:36.494 --> 01:49:39.930
Standing by. Ark 6, stand by.
Ark 7, stand by.


01:49:39.965 --> 01:49:42.603
This is Carl Anheuser
acting CIC on 4,


01:49:42.604 --> 01:49:43.209
Yes sir


01:49:43.210 --> 01:49:45.282
Requesting emergency
conference T-99.


01:50:05.297 --> 01:50:06.996
He thinks the world of
you, you know that?


01:50:09.560 --> 01:50:11.421
He's a great little man.


01:50:12.159 --> 01:50:13.245
Yeah


01:50:21.241 --> 01:50:23.119
I always wanted to have
a family of my own.


01:50:27.063 --> 01:50:28.726
You're a lucky
man, Jackson.


01:50:30.089 --> 01:50:31.393
Don't ever forget it.


01:50:33.522 --> 01:50:35.273
CHO MING UTILITY GATE


01:50:47.102 --> 01:50:48.149
Who are they?


01:50:48.611 --> 01:50:50.282
We found them alongside
of the road.


01:50:50.283 --> 01:50:52.234
Send them back!


01:50:57.802 --> 01:50:59.479
I am a follower


01:51:00.227 --> 01:51:02.203
of our great
Lama Rinpoche.


01:51:02.902 --> 01:51:04.312
You know I cannot do that.


01:51:05.758 --> 01:51:07.255
You don't have to
take all of us.


01:51:07.256 --> 01:51:08.344
Please just take
my children.


01:51:08.345 --> 01:51:09.593
I'm begging you.


01:51:09.989 --> 01:51:11.548
Why should
I do that?


01:51:11.549 --> 01:51:15.453
Same reason you
sent for your family.


01:51:15.890 --> 01:51:18.363
Please just the children,
you don't have to take us.


01:51:18.364 --> 01:51:19.324
Please!


01:51:21.960 --> 01:51:25.154
Please. Oh my God.


01:51:27.707 --> 01:51:31.391
Please. I don't know if you can
understand what I'm saying.


01:51:31.392 --> 01:51:33.967
As a mother,
I'm begging you.


01:51:33.968 --> 01:51:35.408
Please take them.


01:51:36.666 --> 01:51:37.647
Please.


01:51:40.033 --> 01:51:43.240
We are all children
of the Earth.


01:51:44.030 --> 01:51:47.360
My plan will not work
for so many, Grandma.


01:51:47.361 --> 01:51:51.139
We will take them all.


01:52:05.675 --> 01:52:09.726
Attention.
All construction workers.


01:52:12.318 --> 01:52:14.188
They're opening
the mountain.


01:52:14.189 --> 01:52:17.371
They are leaving
without us.


01:52:18.486 --> 01:52:20.211
Get back. What did
I tell you!


01:52:20.212 --> 01:52:24.057
They are leaving
you behind too.


01:52:24.058 --> 01:52:25.328
<i>Please be patient</i>


01:52:36.996 --> 01:52:39.233
Follow me.


01:52:45.293 --> 01:52:46.728
We have to hurry!


01:52:46.729 --> 01:52:47.997
They are leaving!


01:52:50.648 --> 01:52:52.995
Initiating security
procedures.


01:52:58.168 --> 01:53:00.744
Excuse me. Where can I
find Adrian Helmsley?


01:53:00.745 --> 01:53:02.083
He's on the bridge.
This way.


01:53:06.159 --> 01:53:07.335
Tenzin wait!


01:53:08.667 --> 01:53:10.608
Grandma, we're
almost there.


01:53:10.801 --> 01:53:12.741
Green lights on
pressure, Mr Anton?


01:53:12.742 --> 01:53:14.507
Green lights across
the board, Captain.


01:53:26.144 --> 01:53:27.340
Why do they
have anchors?


01:53:27.341 --> 01:53:30.383
Because they're not
space ships. They're Arcs.


01:53:30.846 --> 01:53:31.950
Let's go.


01:53:43.892 --> 01:53:45.249
Mr President.


01:53:46.237 --> 01:53:47.214
You've got to see this.


01:54:16.679 --> 01:54:18.823
Stop.


01:54:26.817 --> 01:54:28.310
Engage the support
mechanisms.


01:54:28.311 --> 01:54:30.906
Aye-aye, Captain.
Engaging supports.


01:54:30.907 --> 01:54:32.130
Just exactly how long
are these things


01:54:32.131 --> 01:54:33.656
expected to hold us
in place, Captain?


01:54:33.657 --> 01:54:34.519
They're just meant
to withstand the


01:54:34.520 --> 01:54:37.352
first impact of the
waves, Mr Anheuser.


01:54:53.895 --> 01:54:56.740
Down there Oleg,
you go first.


01:55:01.790 --> 01:55:02.986
Caesar!


01:55:22.901 --> 01:55:26.186
Good boy.
Come to Mommy.


01:55:26.187 --> 01:55:27.240
Caesar!


01:55:27.974 --> 01:55:30.026
Mommy, where's Tamara?


01:55:32.228 --> 01:55:33.937
Daddy look!


01:55:36.668 --> 01:55:38.350
Tamara!


01:56:13.352 --> 01:56:16.781
Oh my god, what's
happening out there?


01:56:17.531 --> 01:56:20.629
Anheuser convinced the other
heads of state to launch.


01:56:23.845 --> 01:56:25.420
Mr. Anheuser


01:56:27.070 --> 01:56:29.011
We have to stop
this madness.


01:56:29.799 --> 01:56:31.723
Make sure the other
bridges can see me.


01:56:32.516 --> 01:56:33.091
What do you think
you're doing?


01:56:33.092 --> 01:56:34.457
I know exactly
what I'm doing.


01:56:37.031 --> 01:56:39.030
Ladies and Gentleman,
this is Dr. Adrian Helmsley


01:56:39.032 --> 01:56:42.111
Chief science adviser to
the late President Wilson.


01:56:42.212 --> 01:56:44.871
Could you please turn up
the volume, Mr Hoffman.


01:56:45.062 --> 01:56:46.070
I know we've all
been forced to make


01:56:46.071 --> 01:56:49.274
difficult decisions to save
our human civilization.


01:56:49.275 --> 01:56:51.968
But to be human means
to care for each other


01:56:52.002 --> 01:56:53.973
and civilization means
to work together


01:56:53.974 --> 01:56:55.908
to create a better life.


01:56:56.041 --> 01:56:58.261
If that's true, then
there's nothing human


01:56:58.262 --> 01:57:01.235
and nothing civilized about
what we're doing here.


01:57:01.236 --> 01:57:03.728
Dr. Helmsley's passion
is admirable,


01:57:03.862 --> 01:57:06.454
But I remind you that
we have very limited


01:57:06.455 --> 01:57:08.159
resources and extremely
limited time.


01:57:08.160 --> 01:57:09.855
Ask yourselves, can
we really stand by


01:57:09.856 --> 01:57:12.957
and watch these
people die?


01:57:13.346 --> 01:57:15.362
I read a quote
two days ago.


01:57:15.465 --> 01:57:17.698
The author is probably
dead by now. But he said:


01:57:17.699 --> 01:57:20.074
"The moment we stop
fighting for each other"


01:57:20.078 --> 01:57:23.379
"Thats the moment that
we lose our humanity"


01:57:23.465 --> 01:57:24.655
And in order to save
the human race,


01:57:24.656 --> 01:57:27.163
we have and obligation
to stick to this plan


01:57:27.198 --> 01:57:30.289
which every nation on this
flotilla signed up for.


01:57:30.290 --> 01:57:32.650
They're in God's
hands now.


01:57:34.433 --> 01:57:36.843
Officer, you turn that off.


01:57:37.791 --> 01:57:38.959
That is an order,
sailor. Turn it off!


01:57:38.994 --> 01:57:40.674
Don't you dare touch
that button, young man!


01:57:40.675 --> 01:57:43.488
Have you completely
lost your mind?


01:57:43.816 --> 01:57:44.735
Look at the clock!


01:57:44.914 --> 01:57:47.373
We have barely
15 minutes left!


01:57:47.647 --> 01:57:48.394
Do you want to be
responsible for the


01:57:48.395 --> 01:57:49.966
extinction of the
human race?


01:57:49.967 --> 01:57:51.367
Can you handle
that, Adrian?


01:57:52.023 --> 01:57:54.168
There's a young astrophysicist
from India who's the


01:57:54.169 --> 01:57:55.345
reason we are all here.


01:57:55.346 --> 01:57:56.994
Oh, for God's sake.


01:57:57.145 --> 01:57:59.584
He's the one who
discovered it all.


01:57:59.585 --> 01:58:03.165
He connected all the dots,
we all owe him our lives.


01:58:03.268 --> 01:58:04.557
I just learned that
he was killed with


01:58:04.558 --> 01:58:08.481
his family in a Tsunami
in eastern India.


01:58:09.987 --> 01:58:12.178
He was my friend.


01:58:12.776 --> 01:58:15.009
And he died in vain.


01:58:15.341 --> 01:58:18.373
Everybody out there
has died in vain.


01:58:18.516 --> 01:58:22.385
If we start our future
with an act of cruelty,


01:58:23.671 --> 01:58:28.933
what will you tell
your children?


01:58:31.273 --> 01:58:35.180
If my father were here,
he would open the gates


01:58:41.644 --> 01:58:44.162
The people of Russia
along with...


01:58:45.175 --> 01:58:46.435
China


01:58:48.212 --> 01:58:49.948
and Japan


01:58:49.949 --> 01:58:50.909
Agree


01:58:52.248 --> 01:58:54.489
To open the gates!


01:58:55.884 --> 01:59:00.112
The United Kingdom, Spain,
France and Germany,


01:59:00.116 --> 01:59:02.454
and I believe I may
also speak for the


01:59:02.455 --> 01:59:04.381
Italian Prime Minister:


01:59:04.645 --> 01:59:08.306
We vote to let these
people come in.


01:59:13.095 --> 01:59:15.249
Captain Michaels.


01:59:16.226 --> 01:59:18.800
Please


01:59:21.055 --> 01:59:22.613
This is your Captain.


01:59:22.614 --> 01:59:26.072
In a few moments,
we will open the gates.


01:59:32.941 --> 01:59:35.616
Phew, it stinks.


01:59:53.380 --> 01:59:55.690
They are opening
the gate. Come down!


01:59:55.691 --> 01:59:57.551
Noah. Move it!


01:59:58.075 --> 02:00:00.718
Noah! Noah!


02:00:11.011 --> 02:00:13.013
Mom, something happened.


02:00:20.399 --> 02:00:22.829
Come on, God damn it!
Give me your hand!


02:00:22.830 --> 02:00:26.658
- Reach for it!
- Help me!


02:00:29.009 --> 02:00:31.018
Gordon!


02:00:32.857 --> 02:00:34.504
Stop!


02:00:39.096 --> 02:00:40.578
Climb!


02:01:12.960 --> 02:01:14.191
What's wrong
with the gate?


02:01:14.511 --> 02:01:15.550
Looks like it didn't
run the full cycle.


02:01:15.551 --> 02:01:16.511
We're checking it out.


02:01:18.135 --> 02:01:21.092
Order, please!


02:01:25.326 --> 02:01:28.269
<i>4 minutes to impact</i>


02:02:11.863 --> 02:02:14.881
We're all loaded, Captain.
Then let's lock it up. Now!


02:02:24.427 --> 02:02:27.674
Oleg! Grab
my hand!


02:02:39.109 --> 02:02:45.344
No, no, no


02:02:56.759 --> 02:02:58.087
HYDRAULIC MALFUNCTION


02:02:58.284 --> 02:02:59.863
Something's jamming the
hydraulics, Captain.


02:03:00.004 --> 02:03:01.116
Well then get it out
for Christ sake.


02:03:01.117 --> 02:03:02.463
I can't fire up the
engines until we


02:03:02.464 --> 02:03:03.901
get a good seal
on that gate.


02:03:04.758 --> 02:03:07.099
Captain, we have a breach
in the zoological bay.


02:03:07.244 --> 02:03:09.268
Can you zoom in?
- Yeah.


02:03:13.294 --> 02:03:14.237
I know those kids.


02:03:14.239 --> 02:03:16.679
What is happening?
What's going on?


02:03:16.908 --> 02:03:18.673
Where did they
come from?


02:03:20.461 --> 02:03:22.401
There. Through the
hydraulic chamber.


02:03:22.530 --> 02:03:23.784
Captain, I think we
found the problem!


02:03:23.785 --> 02:03:26.270
- Who are these people?
- No, wait!


02:03:26.676 --> 02:03:27.466
He's injured.


02:03:27.832 --> 02:03:31.403
Something must've
gone wrong.


02:03:31.438 --> 02:03:34.245
Are you kidding me? Of course
something went wrong!


02:03:34.257 --> 02:03:36.061
Congratulations to
the both of you.


02:03:36.125 --> 02:03:37.295
Might have gotten us
all killed, but as long


02:03:37.296 --> 02:03:39.461
as your conscience is
clean, right Helmsley?


02:03:39.462 --> 02:03:41.430
Captain, get an emergency
team down there,


02:03:41.431 --> 02:03:43.114
I'll meet them at the
hydraulics chamber.


02:03:43.115 --> 02:03:44.983
You know your way
around here? Lets go!


02:03:45.120 --> 02:03:47.355
<i>1 minute to impact.</i>


02:04:00.344 --> 02:04:01.084
Captain?


02:04:01.553 --> 02:04:03.481
Cho Ming airfield
has been hit.


02:04:03.800 --> 02:04:07.694
Put me on emergency
comm, Mr Taylor.


02:04:08.154 --> 02:04:10.278
This is the Captain speaking


02:04:10.339 --> 02:04:13.010
We expect to be impacted
by water shortly.


02:04:13.202 --> 02:04:17.951
We need to
go this way.


02:04:35.004 --> 02:04:38.136
All stations prepare
for impact.


02:05:21.885 --> 02:05:24.296
Pressure just climbed
80 Pascal.


02:05:24.299 --> 02:05:27.024
Surface compression of
valve sensors, Captain.


02:05:27.026 --> 02:05:29.378
Track Dr Helmsley.


02:05:34.013 --> 02:05:36.818
Out of the way!
Excuse me.


02:05:37.511 --> 02:05:39.735
Tenzin. Almost there.


02:05:40.381 --> 02:05:42.046
Nima. What happened?


02:05:44.042 --> 02:05:44.944
Tamara!


02:05:44.945 --> 02:05:47.286
Will you take
the kids please?


02:05:47.605 --> 02:05:48.708
Which way?


02:05:48.891 --> 02:05:52.930
We can't get there!
Water is entering the stern.


02:05:52.964 --> 02:05:55.094
The rear of this ship is
flooded and will seal up


02:05:55.113 --> 02:05:56.667
one compartment
at a time.


02:05:57.000 --> 02:05:58.457
Where's Gordon?


02:05:59.722 --> 02:06:00.735
No?


02:06:02.675 --> 02:06:04.829
We gotta go back!


02:06:04.830 --> 02:06:06.462
We have to go back!


02:06:09.890 --> 02:06:11.078
Mommy!


02:06:12.018 --> 02:06:13.428
Help!
Mommy!


02:06:15.820 --> 02:06:18.371
Run!


02:06:21.948 --> 02:06:25.509
Go over, Lilly!


02:06:26.323 --> 02:06:28.662
Caesar!
Lilly, take him!


02:06:30.758 --> 02:06:32.825
Mommy!


02:06:39.531 --> 02:06:41.781
Is there another way to
the hydraulics chamber?


02:06:41.998 --> 02:06:42.915
Where does this ladder go?


02:06:42.950 --> 02:06:45.932
- To the zoological pens
- Okay, let's go!


02:06:51.566 --> 02:06:54.955
Professor?
It's Air Force One.


02:07:11.401 --> 02:07:13.164
The mid-ship anchor
support is hit.


02:07:13.244 --> 02:07:14.244
Can you stabilize it?


02:07:14.245 --> 02:07:16.013
The bow anchor
is giving in.


02:07:34.661 --> 02:07:36.651
Captain, the turbines
aren't responding.


02:07:36.652 --> 02:07:39.565
So override it.
Hit the override.


02:07:39.598 --> 02:07:41.333
We cant start the engine
until we close that gate.


02:07:58.960 --> 02:08:01.357
Help me!
Help!


02:08:06.419 --> 02:08:10.261
Momma!


02:08:10.295 --> 02:08:12.050
- Are you OK?
- My mommy is in there.


02:08:12.051 --> 02:08:13.011
Please help her!


02:08:13.012 --> 02:08:13.836
We'll get to your
mommy, sweetheart.


02:08:13.837 --> 02:08:15.549
They're doing everything
they can, okay?


02:08:15.550 --> 02:08:16.667
Can we talk to her?


02:08:16.702 --> 02:08:18.668
I'm gonna try
to connect us.


02:08:18.701 --> 02:08:20.217
We have to stop
the bleeding!


02:08:20.218 --> 02:08:21.370
How about my belt?


02:08:21.561 --> 02:08:24.407
- Here Mom!
- Mr. Curtis? Jackson?


02:08:25.695 --> 02:08:27.586
Help! Hey!


02:08:27.620 --> 02:08:29.926
It's Adrian Helmsley,
we met at Yellowstone.


02:08:29.959 --> 02:08:32.443
Thats great. Open
the God damn door!


02:08:32.476 --> 02:08:34.231
Your daughter
is with me!


02:08:34.265 --> 02:08:37.357
- Lilly?
- Where's Noah?


02:08:37.390 --> 02:08:39.147
I'm right here, Lil!


02:08:39.148 --> 02:08:41.037
<i>Impact warning</i>


02:08:41.072 --> 02:08:44.602
<i>30° West.
45° East.</i>


02:08:44.603 --> 02:08:48.271
<i>Target elevation
29.035 feet.</i>


02:08:48.272 --> 02:08:51.410
29.000 feet? What the
hell is at 29.000 feet?


02:08:51.444 --> 02:08:53.174
We're headed straight
for the north face


02:08:53.175 --> 02:08:55.679
of Mount Everest,
Mr. Anheuser.


02:08:55.713 --> 02:08:57.757
And if we can't
start our engines,


02:08:57.758 --> 02:08:59.730
we will not survive
the impact.


02:09:09.489 --> 02:09:12.566
Jackson, you're sealed off!
We can't get to you!


02:09:12.567 --> 02:09:14.415
There's something
blocking the hydraulics


02:09:14.416 --> 02:09:16.992
If you can't get it out,
none of us are gonna make it


02:09:18.030 --> 02:09:20.373
Dr Helmsley,
look at this.


02:09:20.976 --> 02:09:23.100
It's completely submerged
down there and there's


02:09:23.101 --> 02:09:24.699
no way for them
to get any air.


02:09:24.700 --> 02:09:25.878
Theres no other way!


02:09:25.879 --> 02:09:28.169
But it's a suicide
mission, sir!


02:09:35.104 --> 02:09:37.552
I know where it is,
I'll give it a try.


02:09:43.733 --> 02:09:46.219
Dad, wait, I wanna
go with you!


02:09:46.284 --> 02:09:48.836
- Dad, I wanna help you!
- No, no, no.


02:09:48.837 --> 02:09:50.870
- You are helping me.
- Dad, please!


02:09:50.903 --> 02:09:53.285
Remember when Lilly
was born and you wanted


02:09:53.286 --> 02:09:55.359
to be introduced
as her big brother?


02:09:55.514 --> 02:09:56.896
Well, she's scared now.


02:09:56.897 --> 02:09:58.756
She needs you
more than ever.


02:09:58.758 --> 02:10:01.938
If you're safe, I know that
she's safe. Do you understand?


02:10:08.172 --> 02:10:10.182
You can help me out
the next time.


02:10:12.957 --> 02:10:14.878
We caused this thing,
it was us.


02:10:14.879 --> 02:10:16.663
I gotta go
check it out.


02:10:45.662 --> 02:10:47.413
Can you hear me?


02:10:50.742 --> 02:10:52.363
No


02:11:18.142 --> 02:11:19.209
Press down!


02:11:19.242 --> 02:11:21.011
Press down with
your hand!


02:11:28.899 --> 02:11:31.260
Don't stop.
Keep pressing!


02:11:47.291 --> 02:11:50.665
No!


02:11:52.490 --> 02:11:57.117
<i>Distance to impact:
1.850 meters</i>


02:11:59.389 --> 02:12:00.511
There he is!


02:12:02.024 --> 02:12:03.649
- Captain!
- We have a visual!


02:12:03.684 --> 02:12:05.274
I think we found
the problem.


02:12:05.275 --> 02:12:07.273
Show us the
hydraulics chamber


02:12:23.846 --> 02:12:25.809
God dammit! I told you
to stay up there!


02:12:25.810 --> 02:12:27.116
I just wanted to help.


02:12:27.117 --> 02:12:30.328
Alright. Hold the light.


02:12:30.329 --> 02:12:33.034
We're right under
the air pocket, okay?


02:12:33.035 --> 02:12:34.776
How did you know
I needed help?


02:12:39.507 --> 02:12:42.965
Grandpa, Grandma...
I'm sorry.


02:12:42.999 --> 02:12:44.065
I could not save us


02:12:44.436 --> 02:12:47.749
He has gone back in.
He will fix it.


02:12:48.055 --> 02:12:50.669
There's no way.


02:12:51.218 --> 02:12:53.594
Don't lose faith, brother.


02:13:20.253 --> 02:13:21.868
Dad!


02:13:29.004 --> 02:13:30.182
We're gonna die!


02:13:51.525 --> 02:13:54.517
Great job! You light the way
and I'll go for the cable.


02:13:55.676 --> 02:13:58.438
<i>Distance to impact:
400 meters</i>


02:13:58.439 --> 02:13:59.636
Underwater ridge ahead!


02:13:59.637 --> 02:14:01.015
We're going to run
aground, Captain!


02:14:30.115 --> 02:14:31.838
Sir, the gate is sealed!


02:14:31.839 --> 02:14:33.004
That's affirmative, Captain!


02:14:33.005 --> 02:14:36.908
- Anton, start the engines.
- Aye-aye Captain. Full reverse.


02:14:44.336 --> 02:14:46.471
Captain! We're not
gonna make it!


02:14:46.472 --> 02:14:49.500
<i>Distance to impact:
15 meters.</i>


02:15:13.390 --> 02:15:15.584
Reverse motion
activated


02:15:15.585 --> 02:15:19.058
<i>Distance to impact:
10 meters.</i>


02:15:19.703 --> 02:15:21.183
<i>20 meters.</i>


02:15:34.987 --> 02:15:37.317
Hard to port!


02:15:47.950 --> 02:15:50.308
We did it! We did it!


02:15:50.938 --> 02:15:53.289
- Where's Dad?
- He was right behind me


02:15:54.677 --> 02:15:56.789
Any word from the
hydraulic chamber?


02:15:56.790 --> 02:15:57.598
Where is he?


02:15:57.599 --> 02:15:59.281
I thought you said he
was right behind you.


02:15:59.282 --> 02:15:59.952
He was!


02:15:59.953 --> 02:16:01.805
<i>- Are you sure?
- Yes.</i>


02:16:01.806 --> 02:16:03.608
He was right there!


02:16:11.392 --> 02:16:14.706
Dad. Dad!


02:16:14.707 --> 02:16:17.335
Come on, Jackson.
Come on.


02:16:20.909 --> 02:16:23.552
<i>Please, please.</i>


02:16:25.400 --> 02:16:28.039
Please, please.


02:16:44.525 --> 02:16:45.822
He did it!


02:16:46.089 --> 02:16:47.386
He did it!


02:17:30.217 --> 02:17:37.286
DAY 27 MONTH 01 YEAR 0001


02:17:43.562 --> 02:17:46.413
Shuttle Atlantis.
Our last day.


02:17:46.414 --> 02:17:49.810
All we can hear is the sound
of our own breathing.


02:17:49.811 --> 02:17:51.851
That reminds us we are still


02:17:51.886 --> 02:17:55.113
sharing our memories,
hopes and ideas.


02:17:55.114 --> 02:17:58.525
And isn't it funny?
Just this morning we worked it out


02:17:58.526 --> 02:18:01.859
Somehow or another,
we all have relatives


02:18:01.860 --> 02:18:03.480
in Wisconsin.


02:18:05.819 --> 02:18:07.183
The end.


02:18:16.690 --> 02:18:17.880
It's good.


02:18:18.707 --> 02:18:20.325
I thought you
would like it.


02:18:22.202 --> 02:18:27.702
Tell me Dr Wilson:
Apart from books and art.


02:18:27.703 --> 02:18:28.873
Do you think there's
anything else


02:18:28.874 --> 02:18:29.834
we might possibly share?


02:18:31.222 --> 02:18:33.186
In the future?


02:18:34.068 --> 02:18:37.497
Are you asking me out
on a date, Dr. Helmsley?


02:18:38.272 --> 02:18:41.031
You know my diary
is pretty full.


02:18:42.503 --> 02:18:44.048
Actually...


02:18:46.421 --> 02:18:48.120
Yes, I was.


02:18:52.408 --> 02:18:54.877
<i>Dr. Helmsley to
the bridge, please.</i>


02:18:54.878 --> 02:18:57.122
<i>Dr. Helmsley
to the bridge.</i>


02:18:59.249 --> 02:19:00.650
Come here.


02:19:06.836 --> 02:19:09.237
<i>Ladies and gentleman,
this is captain Michaels speaking.</i>


02:19:09.238 --> 02:19:13.163
<i>In a few minutes I will give
orders to unseal the decks.</i>


02:19:14.333 --> 02:19:17.506
<i>At 23:45 last night,
our sister Arks</i>


02:19:17.541 --> 02:19:20.915
<i>number 6 and 7
have joined our course.</i>


02:19:21.596 --> 02:19:23.274
<i>For the first time
on our journey,</i>


02:19:23.275 --> 02:19:24.235
we will have clear skies.


02:19:26.382 --> 02:19:28.358
<i>As you know our
passenger count</i>


02:19:28.359 --> 02:19:29.319
<i>is way over capacity.</i>


02:19:29.946 --> 02:19:32.472
<i>So please, be careful
when you step out</i>


02:19:32.473 --> 02:19:35.697
<i>and of course...
enjoy the fresh air.</i>


02:19:38.373 --> 02:19:39.770
Can I hold him?


02:19:39.771 --> 02:19:42.858
Sure, he can be your
dog too if you like.


02:19:42.859 --> 02:19:44.093
Thanks.


02:19:47.812 --> 02:19:49.260
Where have you
been all my life?


02:19:49.261 --> 02:19:50.702
Gift shop.


02:20:45.610 --> 02:20:47.839
Oh, Adrian. Excellent.


02:20:47.874 --> 02:20:50.938
I called because we just got
our first satellite feet.


02:20:50.939 --> 02:20:53.368
The equalization of the
oceanic... seabeds


02:20:53.369 --> 02:20:55.917
has not turned out to be
as extreme as we expected.


02:20:55.918 --> 02:20:57.755
The waters are receding.


02:20:57.756 --> 02:20:58.805
Much faster
than we thought.


02:20:58.806 --> 02:21:00.662
Thank God. And...


02:21:00.663 --> 02:21:02.913
This is hard to believe,
but the Himalayas


02:21:02.914 --> 02:21:04.813
are no longer the
roof of the world.


02:21:04.814 --> 02:21:06.688
It's now the
Drakensberg mountains


02:21:06.689 --> 02:21:08.000
of KwaZulu, Nepal.


02:21:08.001 --> 02:21:10.352
The entire African
continent has just risen


02:21:10.353 --> 02:21:12.892
7.000 feet, and unlikely
they are even flooded.


02:21:12.893 --> 02:21:15.597
That's why they call it
The Cape of Good Hope.


02:21:15.598 --> 02:21:17.386
We've already set
course for it.


02:21:24.343 --> 02:21:26.687
Daddy, when will
we go back home?


02:21:26.688 --> 02:21:28.104
Well, we talked
about that.


02:21:28.139 --> 02:21:29.520
We're gonna
find a new home


02:21:29.521 --> 02:21:30.480
out here somewhere.


02:21:30.921 --> 02:21:32.111
Right?


02:21:32.112 --> 02:21:34.861
Wherever we're all
together. That's home.


02:21:34.862 --> 02:21:37.280
Right? You are scared?


02:21:37.281 --> 02:21:38.596
I am not.


02:21:40.517 --> 02:21:42.340
No more pull-ups.


02:21:45.004 --> 02:21:46.448
Nice.

